{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e","id":525825,"title":"The Ordo Dracul in 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-23T13:23:35-07:00","id":525825,"title":"The Ordo Dracul in 2E","content":"So, in the thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2\">Non-Super Evil VtR2</a> I posted this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502310#post502310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem 2E really stepped full-throttle on the &quot;wholly evil&quot; aspect, which was a bit of a turn-off for me. A lot of the new powers, especially Covenant-related, seem to revolve around varying levels of human sacrifice (I honestly don't think I read a single Scale that didn't involve leaving a human dead or severely injured, for just a temporary effect). Really clashes with the semi-optimistic view of Vampires I have in my Chronicle. I mean, yeah, a lot of them are bastards, but a sizeable group are just doing the best they can (or at least want to be seen that way.) Yeah, my Gotham City is run by a Mafia-styled Invictus who keeps the bad people rich and the good people scared to stay in power, but there's a Carthian Movement that's trying to take them down to restore some semblance of freedom and justice. The Carthians in my Minneapolis have a council with representatives from the other supernatural groups, specifically so everyone can try and co-operate, or at least not step on each others' toes. The Invictus of St. Paul aren't really bad, they're just Invictus.<br /> <br /> Thing is, any of the Covenants can really be portrayed as good or bad, depending on your own prejudices and how you want to run the story. Are the Lancea Sanctum really a good vampire church, offering meaning and comfort in an unlife of Damnation? Or are they complete religious zealots, crusading against anything that offends their doctrine and putting all nonbelievers (breathing or not) to the sword? Are the Circle of the Crone just vampiric pagans, seeking to get closer to the truth of nature? Or are they worshipers of dark, possibly demonic spirits that demand tribute in blood? Are the Ordo Dracul learned scholars, delving into the mysteries of the vampiric condition, or are they monsters ascendant, overcoming the few weaknesses that can slow unstoppable juggernauts of blood and death? Do the Invictus represent order and stability, or control and stagnation? Do the Carthians represent freedom and democracy, or anarchy and chaos? It's all in how you choose to interpret them.<br /> <br /> Which I guess is my biggest gripe with a lot of the new mechanics. Playing the Ordo Dracul as learned scholars seeking vampiric enlightenment is a tad difficult when most of their powers stem from research that would make Dr. Mengle say &quot;Dude, that's fucked up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A few people posted in response to say that I was being a bit uncharitable. So, I took another look at the 2E book and. . . well, no, I don't think I am.<br /> <br /> The Ordo really seems to be a bunch of really sick bastards in 2E now. I'd like to share a few things that give me this impression:<br /> <br /> First, in Mysteries of the Dragon, the last line of the first paragraph: &quot;They call the results, refined through rigorous self-control and clear-minded study.&quot; Sounds good so far.<br /> <br /> Then they start talking about Scales, where it says &quot;But these procedures can be brutal, tantamount to torture, and carry side effects both physical and psychological.&quot; Uh, okay. . . so, the Ordo's &quot;clear-minded research&quot; leads to torturing people?<br /> <br /> Again, talking about Scales of the Ascendant, there's the line &quot;Direct exposure to sunlight and fire, sleep deprivation, and medically induced death are common practices.&quot; Oboy. Now, granted, I misread a lot of these statements about Scales as generic research methods in the Coils, and am realizing now they're intended to be two separate things. . . but still. As for the Scales of the Ascendant themselves, Day-Wake conditioning isn't that bad, but Epidermal Shielding Bath requires &quot;blood and pulped human fat.&quot; Now, while you certainly might be able to get those ingredients without killing someone, seems more like the expected route is through, shall we say, <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HumanResources\" target=\"_blank\">human resources</a>. Likewise with Flesh Graft Treatment, requiring (presumably, though never stated as such) live human skin and (explicitly stated) fresh human blood.<br /> <br /> Scales of the Wyrm are stated to be &quot;savage, even by Ordo standards; subjects are dissected,&quot; which sounds plenty evil to me. Augmented Vitae Draught isn't so bad, again, although it could kill a mortal with the aftereffects. Kindred Sense Endowment requires &quot;blood and bone,&quot; and while the source is never specifically stated, by this point, I think we're all again thinking &quot;human resources.&quot; Oh, it also makes a mortal want to drink blood. Groovy. Surgical Heart Removal is. . . actually pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Scales of Voivode specifically calls out &quot;Initiates of the Mystery commit psychological torture.&quot; Which, honestly, makes them sound like Initiates of the other Mysteries, except they do it en route to purposes while for these guys, it is the purpose. Blood Cleansing Ritual is again called out as &quot;tantamount to torture,&quot; but since it &quot;cures&quot; Blood Bonds, I'll give that one a pass. Fealty's Reward is basically straight-up human sacrifice, except the human doesn't stay quite dead. They may become a Draugr, though. Mass Embrace is just terrifying, probably more so for the person doing it. Sanguinary Invigoration. . . again, actually pretty cool.<br /> <br /> But, really, a lot of this seems to say, with brutal clarity, that Dragons are really nasty people who do really nasty things, and how do they maintain a Humanity over one?<br /> <br /> Now, I really do like the Ordo Dracul, and I want to keep liking them in 2E, but with the way Scales are advanced, I find that difficult. I understand that you don't necessarily have to learn or use Scales, but that they are there, and not specifically called out as being the &quot;dark underside&quot; of Coils, leads me to feel the Dragons are characterized less as potentially noble scholars, and more as bloodthirsty butchers using science as an excuse.<br /> <br /> I'd really like to be proven wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:19:08-07:00","id":525914,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I get where your coming from. My reading recollection is a little outdated for vampire 2e, but if I recall my reaction was similar to yours, and my response was to really take the &quot;you can design your own coils and scales, as well as how to advance in scales and coils period&quot; really to heart. Do a fair number of vampires perform what could be considered at or worse than Nazi science experiments? Yeah, but I like to think another fair number have more humane ways of getting ingredients, Like contacts or bribes at your local blood back or plastic surgery clinic. My main issue with the Ordo Dracul (I liked them the most) was that they were initially presented in some opening paragraphs to be really digging the notion of transcending vampiric limitations (implied their natural weaknesses) and the actual coils themselves... really didnt feel they even went in that direction at all. The sun one and the Beast one I think were fine, but Vovoide made no sense to me what-so-ever. Not that I'm saying they would have to only conduct experiments towards those specific goals, in fact I could see plenty of members less concerned with vampiric weaknesses and more with something like manipulating blood bonds, just that having it as a main coil felt like a clash to me. Like I said though, I'm a little fuzzy on the whole thing. I think I might go re-read now and edit this up a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:22:45-07:00","id":525919,"title":"","content":"I can't answer any of your other questions, but on the Humanity point:<br /> <br /> Take appropriate Banes to cancel out the Breaking Points that your research causes. That's how most of my experienced Ordo NPCs have done it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:30:43-07:00","id":525923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e#post525825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd really like to be proven wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I mean, the game is Gothic Horror, so that was to be expected. Why not just keep the effects and change the flavour and how the experiment runs?<br /> Do you mean you'd like the game to move in an optimistic angle then? Like, that vampires are decent folk trying to get by, doing their best to face the occasional threat of a maddened elder or nihilistic Strix?<br /> <br /> I think the Ordo Dracul scales and coils are a sober look at what experiments are <b>really</b> taking place out there without our knowledge. But the Storyteller and the player should have the full picture, know about stuff that doesn't reach the papers or some documentary. I mean, you do know how meat is really made, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 05-23-2015, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:32:46-07:00","id":525932,"title":"","content":"I've never really grasped the idea of the Ordo as being terribly humane to begin with. They're the most alien of the covenants, and border on the scariest parts of transhuman/posthuman philosophy; their intent is to become perfected monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:44:01-07:00","id":525966,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, The Order is a bunch of scientifically minded Kindred looking to study and dissect their condition in order to put it back together in a manner more to their liking. On the other, said condition is <i>being a walking corpse that eats people to survive</i>. You look at that through a microscope and you're probably not going to like what you see or what you need to do to fix it. <br /> <br /> As for Vovoide, the point of that one is the <i>other</i> prong of the Ordo Dracul's research. They're <i>not </i>just about overcoming banes. They never were. They've always had this other angle where they take the powers the condition grants and improve on them. In a way the Coil of the Wyrm encompasses both these aspects. Part of it is controlling the Beast, part of it is making you even nastier when you frenzy. Vovoide is all about improving what blood bonds can do for you. Plus the fourth and fifth dots do trim off slight banes. First by making the sympathy bonuses one-way, so no more relatives getting that pesky discipline use bonuses, and then by making it so you can sire way more childer than before without killing your humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T15:13:49-07:00","id":526009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=525932#post525932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never really grasped the idea of the Ordo as being terribly humane to begin with. They're the most alien of the covenants, and border on the scariest parts of transhuman/posthuman philosophy; their intent is to become perfected monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div> In 1st Ed the coils could be used to help retain your humanity, or mitigate the effects of low humanity:<br /> <br /> <u>Retaining Humanity</u><br /> <br /> Blood Seeps Slowly: means you need less blood, making it easier to keep your humanity.<br /> <br /> Blood of Beasts: you never need to feed on humans, making it easier to keep your humanity.<br /> <br /> Chastise the Beast: Shuts down frenzy, allowing you to avoid humanity reducing actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Ignoring humanity and getting away with it.</u><br /> <br /> Enliven the Face: removed the humanity cap, allowing you to be a monster and still interact normally with mortals.<br /> <br /> Salve the Mind: Helps you stay sane despite low humanity.<br /> <br /> The Sleep of Early Years: Allows you to spend less time in torpor, despite low humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T16:03:58-07:00","id":526042,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's worth pointing out that the Scales are torturous, and like all but one of them only works on other Kindred, and are the kinds of things that the Ordo are doing to each other or two themselves, so no, they don't really torture people, they do science experiments on each other and themselves that are really not very human or humane at all.<br /> <br /> I'll concede that the resources required to use them are ethically dubious to acquire, but I feel like it's worth pointing out that this sort of morally questionable behavior seems to be part and parcel to any kind of science which is on the cutting edge and delving into ethically dubious territory. You call it butchery, they call it a necessary sacrifice in the name of science, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> That said, I imagine they're far more likely to try to acquire medical waste than mess with the potentially disastrous consequences of regularly murdering people to perform their Scales.<br /> <br /> One more thing: As to the point about being &quot;proven wrong&quot; I'm not sure there's much we can do to help you. The Covenants are not humane organizations. They're not made by humans, for humans or to benefit humans, they're made by, for and to the benefit of Kindred. While individual members and local organizations might vary in how they pursue their agendas, on the whole, they're not really human friendly organizations at the best of times. I think it's really important to keep that in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-23-2015, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T16:54:19-07:00","id":526079,"title":"","content":"Leetsepeak hit the high points. <br /> <br /> Basically there's room for a spectrum of Defiant characters, ranging from responsible but fringe scientist, to blood-soaked butcher who uses science as an excuse. <br /> <br /> Scales are on the nasty end, but Scales aren't the end-all and be-all of Ordo Dracul research. They're quick, dirty, costly, but very useful if you can set it up, or are willing to pay the price to make it happen without less callous preparation. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T17:52:55-07:00","id":526128,"title":"","content":"Wow, thanks for the responses.<br /> <br /> I guess the thing that really eats at me is, Scales aren't really described or looked at as something that &quot;shouldn't&quot; be done, they're just kind of there. If there was some more fluff about how they aren't something the &quot;mainstream&quot; Ordo usually practices, or they're meant to be used in a pinch as the lesser of two evils, I wouldn't mind so much. Or if they had been written requiring less in the way of potentially-homicidal ingredients to be used. It still gives me the feeling that, by default, the Ordo is a group of evil scientists, instead of a group of scientists who may have evil individuals.<br /> <br /> Now, yes, the Covenants are not &quot;humane&quot; groups, but the Ordo in particular seem to go out of their way to be nasty. It's more than a little disheartening, especially since I absolutely loved their vibe in 1E, where they were set on surmounting ALL aspects of the curse, even the needs and drives to do evil things. &quot;Becoming a better vampire&quot; does not necessarily equal &quot;becoming a better monster,&quot; though that is a point of debate that could be a very interesting thing for Ordo vampires to discuss. As for acquiring more Banes to offset Humanity triggers for doing bad things. . . that seems completely contrary to the entire Ordo philosophy. They want to get rid of the limitations they already have, not add more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll concede that the resources required to use them are ethically dubious to acquire, but I feel like it's worth pointing out that this sort of morally questionable behavior seems to be part and parcel to any kind of science which is on the cutting edge and delving into ethically dubious territory. You call it butchery, they call it a necessary sacrifice in the name of science, etc. etc. </div> </div> </div>I think this is a rather offensive statement about science and scientists. Even cutting-edge science has a lot of ethics surrounding how it should be done, and scientists in fields that have ethically dubious applications are usually (granted, not always) concerned with their research being used for positive ends. There are certainly outliers, like infamous Nazi doctors, and there's plenty of debate over exactly how ethical the Manhattan Project ended up being, but most scientists believe in expanding knowledge and benefiting humanity (and many think that they're the same thing). Saying the Ordo's methods are &quot;typical&quot; of scientists is. . . I'm sorry, it's appalling. Sure humans (and vampires) can make mistakes, or come to believe that their research is important enough to bend or break a few rules for the &quot;greater good,&quot; but my problem is that the impression I get is that the only rule for the Ordo Dracul is &quot;by any means necessary,&quot; which really makes it difficult to see the group as anything but antagonistic.<br /> <br /> Now, for the record, I have no problem with the idea that some Ordo research and researchers are unethical. I actually could understand the idea that <i>most</i> Ordo research is unethical by <i>human</i> standards. But a lot of what I've pointed out not only seems unethical, but potentially Masquerade-breakingly stupid, even by vampire standards. Even by Ordo standards, some of this stuff has been called out in-text as being particularly brutal. But there still doesn't seem to be an &quot;value judgement&quot; placed on that statement. In other words, it doesn't say to me that &quot;this is what the Ordo does; this is what the Ordo does but doesn't talk about; and this is what the Ordo only does when no one else, even other Dragons, aren't looking.&quot; It doesn't say that these parts of their research are perfectly acceptable, these parts are acceptable but frowned upon, and these are strictly taboo. Modern science has plenty of legal and ethical rules about what you can and can't do in pursuit of knowledge, and the Kindred are just as fond of rules and regulations as humans are, perhaps more so. And the Dragons most of all (at least, in their 1E characterization.) Now, some of that might be the sandbox approach, allowing players and STs to decide exactly how &quot;evil&quot; they want <i>their</i> Ordo to be, but it still would have been nice to have some guideline in the actual text for what the writer's default assumptions were. And, yeah, I get that they had to be under a certain wordcount.<br /> <br /> What I meant when I said &quot;prove me wrong&quot; was that, if you had a different, &quot;less evil&quot; impression of the Ordo Dracul after reading them, please share with me how you arrived at that conclusion. How you feel the Ordo as presented in 2E can be played as a protagonist faction. How you feel my understanding of them as undead Nazi doctors isn't what the text is saying. So far, what I'm hearing is &quot;yeah, they're pretty much assholes. So?&quot; I apologize profusely if that's not what you're saying, but that's what I'm hearing, so please, if I have it wrong, correct me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T18:28:05-07:00","id":526165,"title":"","content":"My impression of the Ordo Dracul is mostly informed by the 1e information on them, so let's be clear about that potential bias up front.<br /> <br /> One of the complaints I'd seen regarding the OD is that they weren't really &quot;mad scientist&quot; enough. There was discussion of their varying methodologies in the covenant book, but there was nothing to back up what that becomes in terms of playing the game, and putting that research to use. Except for the Coils, sure, but those are long term, and low-impact in the sense of having a character trait that you then put to use. The 1e Coils were almost uniformly passive. That doesn't scream vampire scientist tinkering with the workings of the very Curse. There were a couple merits that were mechanical misfits (it eventually came out that the merits relating to the Impaled were from an older draft of the rules, or some such), and the rules for Crucible Nests were neat, but it was missing something, mechanically, to capture that vampiric, transcendent scientist feel. The Mind of the Devouring Wyrm merit chain was excellent, though. I loved that one for the introspective, scientific, almost mentat-like quality the Ordo Dracul could invoke.<br /> <br /> As far as flavor, there were definitely some inhuman elements intrinsic to the OD even then, see Chasing the Dragon's Tail, and any Fontal nest ritual. But overall it, like all the covenants, has room for whatever type of character you want to play. Diverse motivations fit under the same general &quot;goal&quot; umbrella.<br /> <br /> Take that as context for what I saw when I first skimmed the drafts at Gen Con, and then read in depth when <i>Blood and Smoke/</i>2e released. Suddenly the majority of the fluff, description, and night-to-night workings of the OD were the same (mostly), but the mechanics now have this incredible, dark science, <i>active</i> component in the Scales of the Dragon. You can absolutely go full Mengele with it, and the description, as you've quoted, warns that the Scales are grisly business. The 2e write up of the Ordo Dracul is certainly dark. But, I read that as keeping in line with the tone of the game itself. The Ordo Dracul are about results in the general sense, but how far a given Dragon is willing to go to get those results will vary. Just like what any given Invictus will do to rise in the ranks.<br /> <br /> I suppose I read the Scales as another facet of what the Dragons do, but not necessarily the sum total. You could have a squared-away, scientific Dragon who insists on informed consent for his subjects, and gathers materials from willing donors or via medical waste or cadavers as Leetespeak suggested. Or... ya know... Mengele.<br /> <br /> My early experiences with Ordo Dracul players were of mitigating the horrific demands the Curse placed upon them, mostly for reasons of morality, even in the face of a more utilitarian view of the covenant at large. I enjoy the juxtaposition and challenge of trying to maintain Humanity, and being expected to murder a person as an object lesson in observation and unintended consequences.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense at all? Having a hard time pinning down exactly where my impressions are coming from. This is an interesting exercise.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, one other thing. I think my personal impression is that all the covenants are basically &quot;evil,&quot; if you want to boil it down. I think it's an oversimplification, but they're large groups of vampires. In my estimation they start in moral debt and have to work their way out (again, oversimplification, but I hope my point is coming across). Many don't even try. Many give up after a while. Some manage to stay the course, in their various ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 05-23-2015, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T18:28:50-07:00","id":526166,"title":"","content":"Scales are not an optional part of Ordo... It's pretty much written up, that scales are the results of experiments when one is trying to improve upon a Mystery/Coil. So if you're inventing a coil - you're gonna get some Scales in the process. Tho, if you're just learning a Mystery from a teacher, you might simply learn the Coil without the Scales. <br /> <br /> As for how they can be the protagonists? Simple, like other covenants. When you look at them from their most evil standpoint (as we are looking at ordo right now) all of the covenants are evil. But let's look at the covenants (ordo in this case) from the standpoint of &quot;what draws neonates there&quot;. <br /> &quot;Would you like to beat vampirism? Become more than a vampire? No longer play by the same rules? Would you like to learn what vampirism truly is? And be able to change it?&quot; these are all questions which might draw protagonists to join the ranks. These are all the idealistic questions with which most of the dragons probably start on their work. And only while trying to achieve them they go to the more &quot;evil&quot; workings of ordo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T18:51:42-07:00","id":526203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526128#post526128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a rather offensive statement about science and scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can call it that, but the massive volume of content created over the years on the ethics that accompany scientific inquiry would suggest that it's a very active debate with divisive opinions on the matter. Either way, my point wasn't to make some silly stereotypical idea of how scientists operate, but to illustrate that the Ordo very clearly occupy a position of scientific inquiry where there is little in the way of recorded ethics or regulations to prevent their science from straying into areas that we humans consider immoral. Whether they'd share that opinion is going to come down to the individual Dragon and whether they care about that sort of thing. The default assumption appears to be that the Ordo isn't overly concerned with the ethics of their science, at least with regards to mortals. Make of that what you will.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T20:31:25-07:00","id":526306,"title":"","content":"Plus the Ordo Dracul does do the same thing, they just sort of move up a level. Instead of trying to benefit humanity, they benefit the vampires of the Ordo Dracul. And their acceptable subjects of experimentation follow that bump. But if you want you could have them experimenting on rats, rabbits and chimps, and be just as good and moral as human scientists who do the same.<br /> <br /> To me it seems as if the descriptions you're keen on pointing out are referring to the experimenters and discoverers, those finding new scales and coils and forging new paths. Many of the Ordo are likely apprentices who would never really rise to such a level, or we'd have a lot more scales and coils. And when it refers to experimenting with direct sunlight and fire, I think that might be referring to vampire subjects.<br /> <br /> Also I'm curious what you found that was, 'potentially Masquerade-breakingly stupid.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-23-2015, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:23:40-07:00","id":526359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526128#post526128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess the thing that really eats at me is, Scales aren't really described or looked at as something that &quot;shouldn't&quot; be done, they're just kind of there. If there was some more fluff about how they aren't something the &quot;mainstream&quot; Ordo usually practices, or they're meant to be used in a pinch as the lesser of two evils, I wouldn't mind so much. Or if they had been written requiring less in the way of potentially-homicidal ingredients to be used. It still gives me the feeling that, by default, the Ordo is a group of evil scientists, instead of a group of scientists who may have evil individuals.<br /> <br /> Now, yes, the Covenants are not &quot;humane&quot; groups, but the Ordo in particular seem to go out of their way to be nasty. It's more than a little disheartening, especially since I absolutely loved their vibe in 1E, where they were set on surmounting ALL aspects of the curse, even the needs and drives to do evil things. &quot;Becoming a better vampire&quot; does not necessarily equal &quot;becoming a better monster,&quot; though that is a point of debate that could be a very interesting thing for Ordo vampires to discuss. As for acquiring more Banes to offset Humanity triggers for doing bad things. . . that seems completely contrary to the entire Ordo philosophy. They want to get rid of the limitations they already have, not add more.<br /> <br /> Now, for the record, I have no problem with the idea that some Ordo research and researchers are unethical. I actually could understand the idea that <i>most</i> Ordo research is unethical by <i>human</i> standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe applying human ethical standards to undead monsters who generally wish to transcend their condition without actually becoming human is a particularly productive exercise.<br /> <br /> Simply, the Ordo are not immoral &quot;evil scientists.&quot; They are, however, frighteningly amoral <i>inhuman</i> scientists, who follow a insular, selfish and egocentric philosophy which largely supports the ends justifying the means. The Ordo don't develop and use Scales because they needlessly cause suffering and death. They employ them because in the horror setting that is the nWOD, these gruesome Scales are what actually accomplishes the vampires' goals. The Scales, no matter how unpleasant, work.<br /> <br /> I also hardly find it surprising that Ordo (and most other) vampires would have no compunction against experimenting on or sacrificing the human sheep that serve as little more than their food. By way of comparison, look at what humans are willing to do to various laboratory animals in the name of science for extremely laudable goals. Scientists don't infect animals with disease, observe and then dissect them because the scientists are cruel, they do so because there's nothing more efficient and effective in preventing and treating disease <i>in humans</i>. Of course, suffering is minimized whenever possible, but the research and experiments continue, with objections raised only from only a tiny minority.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, the Ordo's experiments could certainly take their psychological toll on the participating vampires. The Humanity stat is a reflection of this effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, given the Ordo's extensive experience with vampire physiology, I never quite understood why they were unable to choose the Night Doctor Surgery Merit (V 2e, pp. 113-14 ). In many ways, this merit appears more appropriate to many Ordo vampires than to the Carthians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:35:50-07:00","id":526361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526359#post526359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, given the Ordo's extensive experience with vampire physiology, I never quite understood why they were unable to choose the Night Doctor Surgery Merit (V 2e, pp. 113-14 ). In many ways, this merit appears more appropriate to many Ordo vampires than to the Carthians.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be happy to explain why I feel it's more appropriate as a Carthian Merit, but this is an old argument, the kind that tends to spawn pages upon pages of debate and I don't want to derail this thread. So I'll just say that I disagree and if you're interested in discussing it further we should do it in another thread or private messages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T21:47:30-07:00","id":526368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526361#post526361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be happy to explain why I feel it's more appropriate as a Carthian Merit, but this is an old argument, the kind that tends to spawn pages upon pages of debate and I don't want to derail this thread. So I'll just say that I disagree and if you're interested in discussing it further we should do it in another thread or private messages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't often post in the Vampire forums, and had no idea the merit might be a large source of consternation. I also didn't suggest that it should not be a Carthian merit, only that it additionally seems appropriate for the Ordo, particularly given the nature of Ordo experimentation discussed in this thread. In any event, it was a very small aside within my much larger commentary about the amoral Ordo philosophy and procedures, and why I believe the gruesome nature of the Scales is consistent with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T23:22:28-07:00","id":526429,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it seems a bit odd to me to call out the scales of the dragon as particularly &quot;evil,&quot; when three out of the five clan-specific disciplines basically involve inflicting varying levels of psychological abuse. Majesty robs victims of their agency, turning them into dependent sycophants unable to so much as think ill of the vampire. Nightmare inflicts terrifying hallucinations that can shatter a victim's courage and self-confidence. Example commands that can be enforced with the <i>first dot</i> of Dominate include &quot;shoot your husband&quot; and &quot;you killed that man.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sure, the scales of the dragon often involve a more obvious, gross sort of torture or violence, but I suspect that most would be far less psychologically damaging in the long term than any of these disciplines. Opportunities to be monstrous are abundantly available to all vampires, regardless of covenant; the onus is on the individual character to decide how much evil they're willing to live with, and what powers they'll choose to reject for moral reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 05-24-2015, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T02:57:30-07:00","id":526505,"title":"","content":"As far as more humane methods of harvesting human bits goes the obvious one is to use ghouls and then be generous with the vitae afterwards so they can heal up quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T03:12:44-07:00","id":526506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526505#post526505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as more humane methods of harvesting human bits goes the obvious one is to use ghouls and then be generous with the vitae afterwards so they can heal up quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't believe using blood enslaved, potentially immortal, perpetual organ donors, instead of normal humans, really demonstrably changes the perception of Ordo vampires as more humane or less conventionally &quot;evil.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> (I also don't know if ghouls would necessarily suffice as experimental or source material for most Scales under the current rules)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T08:19:38-07:00","id":526669,"title":"","content":"The Defiant aren't meant to be nice. None of the covenants are. They exist as dogmas - representations of philosophical points on the nature of vampire existence - that ultimately aren't particularly friendly or humane or altruistic. It *should* be challenging for a regular, young vampire (read: player characters, likely) to be part of a covenant and to keep a human mindset for long. That's the point - the covenant offer the devil's deal of temporal power/mystical power/understanding/answers/faith in return for your Humanity. <br /> <br /> One of the many things I liked about the Mekhet clanbook is that Wood demonstrates how it works - how someone who's actually a nice, gentle person ends up joining a vampire cult and becoming a believer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T09:28:59-07:00","id":526764,"title":"","content":"I really hope you're proven <b>right</b>, OP. I very much enjoy a dark overlay for nWoD, and anything which shifts the default stance of Covenants members away from being 'real world moral' is a positive for me. You can take it in the evil direction, though I'd say that's mostly the Sanctified. And even then, the purpose of being evil is very specific - you were damned for a purpose, and that purpose is in service to God for the benefit of his flock. And just because the bar has moved, doesn't mean everyone has to be evil for evil's sake all the time. <br /> <br /> But I can very much see religious concepts of good and evil being one of the first things tossed out the window in a Covenant devoted to vampire blood science. <br /> <br /> And that is not to say individual characters are shifted one way or another automatically. A high humanity Dragon PC just screams dramatic possibilities. And there are kindred who will absolutely try to do all the right things to maintain humanity - invest in humane medical trade for fat/blood, avoid the torture scales, etc. But I would immediately put them in competition with other Defiant who completely ignore that handicap to produce better / quicker / stronger results. And I would put results as the path to status / power / opportunity in the Covenant. <br /> <br /> To put another way, I don't tend to enjoy themes of &quot;<i>Covenant X are the good guys</i>.&quot; - But I can enjoy, &quot;<i>I'm going to try and be a good guy in Covenant X despite the odds and disadvantages it will bring.</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T10:02:09-07:00","id":526805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526165#post526165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression of the Ordo Dracul is mostly informed by the 1e information on them, so let's be clear about that potential bias up front.<br /> <br /> One of the complaints I'd seen regarding the OD is that they weren't really &quot;mad scientist&quot; enough. There was discussion of their varying methodologies in the covenant book, but there was nothing to back up what that becomes in terms of playing the game, and putting that research to use. Except for the Coils, sure, but those are long term, and low-impact in the sense of having a character trait that you then put to use. The 1e Coils were almost uniformly passive. That doesn't scream vampire scientist tinkering with the workings of the very Curse. There were a couple merits that were mechanical misfits (it eventually came out that the merits relating to the Impaled were from an older draft of the rules, or some such), and the rules for Crucible Nests were neat, but it was missing something, mechanically, to capture that vampiric, transcendent scientist feel. The Mind of the Devouring Wyrm merit chain was excellent, though. I loved that one for the introspective, scientific, almost mentat-like quality the Ordo Dracul could invoke.<br /> <br /> As far as flavor, there were definitely some inhuman elements intrinsic to the OD even then, see Chasing the Dragon's Tail, and any Fontal nest ritual. But overall it, like all the covenants, has room for whatever type of character you want to play. Diverse motivations fit under the same general &quot;goal&quot; umbrella.<br /> <br /> Take that as context for what I saw when I first skimmed the drafts at Gen Con, and then read in depth when <i>Blood and Smoke/</i>2e released. Suddenly the majority of the fluff, description, and night-to-night workings of the OD were the same (mostly), but the mechanics now have this incredible, dark science, <i>active</i> component in the Scales of the Dragon. You can absolutely go full Mengele with it, and the description, as you've quoted, warns that the Scales are grisly business. The 2e write up of the Ordo Dracul is certainly dark. But, I read that as keeping in line with the tone of the game itself. The Ordo Dracul are about results in the general sense, but how far a given Dragon is willing to go to get those results will vary. Just like what any given Invictus will do to rise in the ranks.<br /> <br /> I suppose I read the Scales as another facet of what the Dragons do, but not necessarily the sum total. You could have a squared-away, scientific Dragon who insists on informed consent for his subjects, and gathers materials from willing donors or via medical waste or cadavers as Leetespeak suggested. Or... ya know... Mengele.<br /> <br /> My early experiences with Ordo Dracul players were of mitigating the horrific demands the Curse placed upon them, mostly for reasons of morality, even in the face of a more utilitarian view of the covenant at large. I enjoy the juxtaposition and challenge of trying to maintain Humanity, and being expected to murder a person as an object lesson in observation and unintended consequences.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense at all? Having a hard time pinning down exactly where my impressions are coming from. This is an interesting exercise.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, one other thing. I think my personal impression is that all the covenants are basically &quot;evil,&quot; if you want to boil it down. I think it's an oversimplification, but they're large groups of vampires. In my estimation they start in moral debt and have to work their way out (again, oversimplification, but I hope my point is coming across). Many don't even try. Many give up after a while. Some manage to stay the course, in their various ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually really good. You raise some excellent points here.<br /> <br /> I absolutely support the idea that individuals in a Covenant, and even a Covenant as a whole, can be placed on the Sliding Scale of Morality wherever the ST and players think they fit best, or need them to be for the story. My objection with the Ordo in 2E (and maybe the other Covenants. . . haven't read as deeply into them because I'm mostly stuck with what I did with them in 1E in my ongoing game) is that they seem to be, as Smarmy suggests, planted farther on the &quot;dark&quot; side by default then they had been previously. It's not that it's impossible to play them as &quot;good guys,&quot; but it seems more difficult and inherently against what the book makes them out to be.<br /> <br /> But I think we've touched on something that does spark my interest now. . . exploring the ideas of when ends justify means. What rules and codes are the Dragons willing to break in the name of progress, and when do they decide that a path of research is too unethical to pursue? If something seems promising enough, will they allow wholesale slaughter, or will they stop shy of a potentially paradigm-altering discovery because the means to get there are distasteful?<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of a first season episode of Babylon 5, in which a Dilgar (evil alien race) shows up on the station. She's a famed war criminal among race noted for war crimes, but is soon being protected by every major faction on the station, since she has an immortality formula. Turns out, her formula requires a key ingredient that cannot be synthesized, it must be harvested from living, sentient beings. She goes on to explain that those who have it will destroy those who don't to keep living forever, and her work will reshape the galaxy in her image. Instead of destroying it and her, Commander Sinclair follows his orders and transports her to Earth. . . and a Vorlon ship intercepts her just as she leaves the station and blows her up, with Kosh stating that &quot;You are not ready for immortality.&quot;<br /> <br /> That kind of questioning seems very interesting to me. What ethical guidelines do the Ordo place on the research, and are they times when they break them because the potential rewards are too valuable? Hopefully, that kind of thing can be expanded on in 2E Covenant books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T10:45:46-07:00","id":526827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526805#post526805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually really good. You raise some excellent points here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic, I'm glad.<br /> <br /> Personally I like the dark pall that's been cast over the Ordo Dracul, as it was easy for them to kind of get lost in the science and shuffled off to the side, previously. Though I also think it's a disservice to think that this slight re-imagining, and it is slight, shuts down the moral or ethical play style. They're easily my favorite covenant continuing into 2e, though I certainly see where you're coming from with the tonal shift. I get why that is off-putting to some.<br /> <br /> It's funny that you bring up that episode of Babylon 5. That's the only full episode of the show that I've seen, and I love it. Sounds like you've hit on a hook to make the Ordo Dracul interesting, compelling, and workable in your games.<br /> <br /> With the inherent structure set up in the OD (assuming you keep the rank/title breakdown more or less intact from 1e, and I don't see any compelling reason not to, despite the thought that all 1e books are null and void that occasionally pops up) you can explore the ethical and moral boundaries of the Mysteries along both personal and political axes. What are you willing to do? What are you willing to do to make sure your superiors don't shut you down, or your colleagues can't steal/sabotage your research?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T12:03:49-07:00","id":526903,"title":"","content":"I think the Ordo coming off as darker overall in 2e than they did in 1e is part of a Requeiem-wide tonal shift. Or... Not really a shift, so much as a refinement. 1e was all over the place in the beginning, and as the game went on, it steadily narrowed its focus as of developed its own identity. But by the time it had figured out where it wanted to go, all the old material was still out there, coloring people's impressions of the game. When 2e released, it had the benefit of starting off where 1e took almost 10 years to end up. From day 1, 2e has been about the slow descent into monstrousness. For some people, that's reading as &quot;all vampires are complete monsters in 2e&quot;, and I don't think that's the intent. I think what the writers are going for is &quot;all vampires constantly struggle with the potential to become complete monsters.&quot; The Scales are there as an example of what a Defiant doctor can become, if they give up on their humanity and abandon their ethics. Remember, these scientists don't start out doing these horrific experiments from day 1. They started out as humans, with human values and human morals. Over time, they began to lose touch with their human nature. As a player, you get to decide if your character goes down that same path, or if she keeps up the fight to hold on to her fleeting Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T16:19:03-07:00","id":527139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526903#post526903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Ordo coming off as darker overall in 2e than they did in 1e is part of a Requeiem-wide tonal shift. Or... Not really a shift, so much as a refinement. 1e was all over the place in the beginning, and as the game went on, it steadily narrowed its focus as of developed its own identity. But by the time it had figured out where it wanted to go, all the old material was still out there, coloring people's impressions of the game. When 2e released, it had the benefit of starting off where 1e took almost 10 years to end up. From day 1, 2e has been about the slow descent into monstrousness. For some people, that's reading as &quot;all vampires are complete monsters in 2e&quot;, and I don't think that's the intent. I think what the writers are going for is &quot;all vampires constantly struggle with the potential to become complete monsters.&quot; The Scales are there as an example of what a Defiant doctor can become, if they give up on their humanity and abandon their ethics. Remember, these scientists don't start out doing these horrific experiments from day 1. They started out as humans, with human values and human morals. Over time, they began to lose touch with their human nature. As a player, you get to decide if your character goes down that same path, or if she keeps up the fight to hold on to her fleeting Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, that makes a lot of sense, and is what I was driving at with my earlier post. The conflict of &quot;how monstrous do we choose to be in pursuit of our goals&quot; is great meat for a story there. I guess I just wish it had been more explicitly called out in the 2E book, though I understand that word count constraints probably contributed to that. Like I said, I hope 2E Covenant books expand on ways to run the Covenants as virtuous, vile, and everything in between, based on the needs of a given story.<br /> <br /> Smarmy: Babylon 5 is probably one of the best sci-fi shows ever made. If you get a chance to watch all five seasons, DO IT.<br /> <br /> Too bad the one OD character in my campaign moved on, they probably won't factor into the Chronicle at all. Which is a shame, since I do love their ideal, and now have a solid idea how I'd go about running them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:09:02-07:00","id":527753,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526128#post526128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the thing that really eats at me is, Scales aren't really described or looked at as something that &quot;shouldn't&quot; be done, they're just kind of there. If there was some more fluff about how they aren't something the &quot;mainstream&quot; Ordo usually practices, or they're meant to be used in a pinch as the lesser of two evils, I wouldn't mind so much. Or if they had been written requiring less in the way of potentially-homicidal ingredients to be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the impression I always got; that anyone with Coils or Scales spends a fair amount of time gory to the elbows. Since unique Disciplines are a big part of the Covenants' payout, it makes it feel like all this non-consensual body horror is the rule rather than the exception. <br /> <br /> Not that you <i>couldn't</i> spend time, resources, and vast amounts of personal pain to make the whole thing less concentration-camp-doctor, of course, but the baseline assumption seems to be pretty part-time mad science hobbyist, at <i>least</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526359#post526359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nevertheless, the Ordo's experiments could certainly take their psychological toll on the participating vampires. The Humanity stat is a reflection of this effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems kind of askew that the Circle gets a hard Breaking Point for engaging in primal predator/prey philosophy, protomonster worship and <i>daaark maaagic</i>, while a Covenant whose unique powers blithely discuss human vivisection, self-experimentation (with all the Breaking Points those both imply) and trans'human'ism as fluff text doesn't. I keep wondering whether it's an oversight or a deliberate design choice, or whether I've just completely lost my mind and can't see the point in front of my face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:18:46-07:00","id":527758,"title":"","content":"The issue with Cruac capping Humanity is that the practitioner has to actively engage and strengthen the Beast to make it work. <br /> <br /> The Coils don't arise directly from the Beast, the way Cruac does. The Defiant risk detachment because of the nasty shit they very likely engage in to make breakthroughs, but they aren't slicing off parts of their nature to feed the Beast. They're trying to get a handle on the Beast so they'll never be at its mercy again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:25:44-07:00","id":527764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=526203#post526203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can call it that, but the massive volume of content created over the years on the ethics that accompany scientific inquiry would suggest that it's a very active debate with divisive opinions on the matter. Either way, my point wasn't to make some silly stereotypical idea of how scientists operate, but to illustrate that the Ordo very clearly occupy a position of scientific inquiry where there is little in the way of recorded ethics or regulations to prevent their science from straying into areas that we humans consider immoral. Whether they'd share that opinion is going to come down to the individual Dragon and whether they care about that sort of thing. The default assumption appears to be that the Ordo isn't overly concerned with the ethics of their science, at least with regards to mortals. Make of that what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>It always struck in my mind that most of the Ordo members would be appalled by the &quot;experiments&quot; via the Axis powers not due to ethics but out of lack of academic rigor and discipline. Not out of the fact that people are harmed so much as there is little academic value out of such an atrocity.<br /> <br /> The <i>Blue</i> and <i>Orange Morality </i>indeed. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:30:53-07:00","id":527767,"title":"","content":"Go back and re-read about how characters develop Scales. If you're doing that, your Breaking Points are capped, at best, as Humanity 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:43:39-07:00","id":527772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=527764#post527764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It always struck in my mind that most of the Ordo members would be appalled by the &quot;experiments&quot; via the Axis powers not due to ethics but out of lack of academic rigor and discipline. Not out of the fact that people are harmed so much as there is little academic value out of such an atrocity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I basically agree with your perspective, but would add that I wouldn't be entirely surprised if some members of the Ordo were formerly the people who were performing the Axis &quot;experiments,&quot; only they were the ones who were able to discern &quot;useful&quot; discoveries and techniques, and might even be the reason they were embraced and joined the Covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T09:58:44-07:00","id":527802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=527758#post527758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Coils don't arise directly from the Beast, the way Cruac does. The Defiant risk detachment because of the nasty shit they very likely engage in to make breakthroughs, but they aren't slicing off parts of their nature to feed the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, instead of trading their Man to their Beast, the Ordo's drifting away from both altogether. They both undergo a transformative process, trading an old identity for something new, and they both engage in questionable (human) moral behavior to do it- the only difference between them is that the Coils and Ordo philosophy aren't tethered directly to a flavor mechanic and to Humanity, respectively, so the implications of both Ordo philosophy and having obtained Coils in the first place kind of get swept under the rug.<br /> <br /> I'm not necessarily saying that it's unbalanced or harmful, mind. It just seems like a peculiar oversight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T10:03:11-07:00","id":527807,"title":"","content":"Learning coils and scales by themselves doesn't do any harm to your Humanity (<i>Performing </i>the latter, maybe). You're just learning what other people figured out. It's doing your <i>own</i> research where things get a bit sticky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T10:10:10-07:00","id":527812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=527807#post527807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Learning coils and scales by themselves doesn't do any harm to your Humanity (<i>Performing </i>the latter, maybe). You're just learning what other people figured out. It's doing your <i>own</i> research where things get a bit sticky.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think much depends on whether learning Coils and Scales has a &quot;lab component&quot; to the process. If so, I can certainly see it as a basis for a lower Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T10:21:08-07:00","id":527818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=527802#post527802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, instead of trading their Man to their Beast, the Ordo's drifting away from both altogether. They both undergo a transformative process, trading an old identity for something new, and they both engage in questionable (human) moral behavior to do it- the only difference between them is that the Coils and Ordo philosophy aren't tethered directly to a flavor mechanic and to Humanity, respectively, so the implications of both Ordo philosophy and having obtained Coils in the first place kind of get swept under the rug.<br /> <br /> I'm not necessarily saying that it's unbalanced or harmful, mind. It just seems like a peculiar oversight.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ordo aren't drifting any farther away from Humanity, intrinsically, by studying the Coils. At least not as they are currently developed. Maybe when someone unlocks the full secret of a Mystery, then sure, Humanity might be left by the wayside at that point. <br /> <br /> As they currently stand, though, the Coils themselves are not inimical to Humanity. Cruac is. It feeds from the strength of the Beast, and is diminished by the strength of the Man, thus the Humanity cap. <br /> <br /> A system by which Coils remove/cap Humanity could be interesting, but it requires a tighter focus on the Defiant end game than is presented in the book. Cool stuff to play with in a given game, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T14:45:10-07:00","id":528111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=527818#post527818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As they currently stand, though, the Coils themselves are not inimical to Humanity. Cruac is. The Ordo aren't drifting any farther away from Humanity, intrinsically, by studying the Coils.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. My point is that given their philosophy, practices, and Discipline, especially when comparing/contrasting them to the Circle's, they <i>probably should </i>:-P<br /> <br /> Oh well. Something else to hock into the Thousand Years of Night pile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T17:42:58-07:00","id":528296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528111#post528111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know. My point is that given their philosophy, practices, and Discipline, especially when comparing/contrasting them to the Circle's, they <i>probably should </i>:-P</div> </div> </div> </div>They shouldn't <i>intrinsically</i> though. Cruac doesn't cap Humanity because it involves doing horrible inhuman things, it caps it because its power comes from the Beast. If you're doing horrible inhuman things in your cruac rituals, you're going to lose Humanity due to <i>Breaking Points</i>. Likewise, if your experiments involve doing horrible inhuman things in the name of science, you're going to lose Humanity due to Breaking Points. But the power of the Coils and Scales does not come directly from the Beast and therefore don't cap Humanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T17:58:29-07:00","id":528305,"title":"","content":"Just double checking to make sure I've got the right context for this thread, the Ordo Dracul basically want to make vampires a better class of monsters, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T18:22:42-07:00","id":528326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528305#post528305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just double checking to make sure I've got the right context for this thread, the Ordo Dracul basically want to make vampires a better class of monsters, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one way to look at it. <br /> <br /> Without a moral judgement (not saying you're being judgmental, just saying that the way you phrased it has certain inherent assumptions, intentional or otherwise), the Ordo Dracul want to be better than they are. Specifically they want all the perks of being a vampire with none of the drawbacks. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T19:57:03-07:00","id":528420,"title":"","content":"Yes, 'class' has some definitions that could be taken the wrong way.<br /> <br /> They're sort of the transhumans of vampires. With the occult knowledge and power to back it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:08:01-07:00","id":528430,"title":"","content":"They're out to overcome the weaknesses inherent in their condition. I like that it specifically calls out, and one point, that a return to humanity is just trading one set of weaknesses for another. You trade being able to walk in the sun and not have a &quot;supernatural mood disorder&quot; for built-in expiration date and potential to shorten that expiration date from disease, poison, and injury.<br /> <br /> Which is part of why the brutality of Scales bothers me. Low humanity can be seen, from certain points of view, as a weakness (though 2E is moving away from that concept, and high humanity can be just as much a weakness, from a certain point of view), so why would the Ordo condone things that cause them to lose it? A dragur is in no position to ascend into something &quot;better than vampire.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:15:34-07:00","id":528438,"title":"","content":"There's the old stock-standard answer of &quot;vampires don't understand the mechanics of breaking points.&quot; <br /> <br /> That's true to a point, but they recognize the results of callous brutality on their psyche, I'm sure. Particularly a covenent full of parasychologists, researchers, undead psychiatrists, and torpor-reading telepaths. <br /> <br /> The other thing you have to keep in mind is that Humanity fluctuates. It drops, it rises. Vampires struggle to hold on to what keeps them anchored in themselves as opposed to sliding down into bloodlust and survival focus. There's even a role within the Ordo Dracul known as the Confessor (to risk treading on Sanctified ground) to keep Dragons on an even keel. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ordo Dracul pg 58</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nature of their experiments and studies frequently calls into question their morality as well as the extent of their ethical boundaries. The more they cross those lines in order to effect some hoped-for scientific accomplishment, the more they risk demolishing what remains of their humanity. By having a Confessor to watch for those dangers, counsel the Dragon how best to avoid them and be there to help her when things go south, the Dragon's Requiem will be marked less by tragedy and more by achievement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things like this are why the 1e covenant books are still worth their weight in gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:19:19-07:00","id":528439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528430#post528430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're out to overcome the weaknesses inherent in their condition. I like that it specifically calls out, and one point, that a return to humanity is just trading one set of weaknesses for another. You trade being able to walk in the sun and not have a &quot;supernatural mood disorder&quot; for built-in expiration date and potential to shorten that expiration date from disease, poison, and injury.<br /> <br /> Which is part of why the brutality of Scales bothers me. Low humanity can be seen, from certain points of view, as a weakness (though 2E is moving away from that concept, and high humanity can be just as much a weakness, from a certain point of view), so why would the Ordo condone things that cause them to lose it? A dragur is in no position to ascend into something &quot;better than vampire.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As another poster indicated earlier, the types of actions necessitated by the Scales will likely stabilize a vampire at around Humanity 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T22:50:39-07:00","id":528558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528430#post528430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is part of why the brutality of Scales bothers me. Low humanity can be seen, from certain points of view, as a weakness (though 2E is moving away from that concept, and high humanity can be just as much a weakness, from a certain point of view), so why would the Ordo condone things that cause them to lose it? A dragur is in no position to ascend into something &quot;better than vampire.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to note that breaking points are not equivalent to Humanity loss. They're a small risk of loss. And with only a few exceptions (one, off the top of my head), a Dragon isn't likely to break lower than Humanity 3-4 by practicing Scales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T03:38:39-07:00","id":528680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528296#post528296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They shouldn't <i>intrinsically</i> though. Cruac doesn't cap Humanity because it involves doing horrible inhuman things, it caps it because its power comes from the Beast.<br /> But the power of the Coils and Scales does not come directly from the Beast and therefore don't cap Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and I <i>get that</i>. I'm saying that the Ordo pushing their inner limits should be leaving their humanity behind because the Beast's influence isn't the <i>only </i>thing that results in Humanity loss. <br /> <br /> You're saying that the Ordo can't have a Humanity cap because their power doesn't come directly from the Beast, because the cap mechanic comes from the Circle, who <i>do</i> get their power from the Beast, yes? <i>I'm</i> saying that regardless of where their power comes from, the mindset that <i>drives </i>it would be accurately represented by a Humanity cap.<br /> <br /> It's not even so much that the Coils and Scales are corruptive (although those Breaking Points are still there), it's that someone dedicated enough to transcend even mundane undeath is probably going to have a lot of 'em, which is kind of the only metric available for that kind of... uh... personal growth. Their relationship is more correlative than causative, but it's there.<br /> <br /> ...or should be, I guess, is my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T03:46:58-07:00","id":528692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528680#post528680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and I <i>get that</i>. I'm saying that the Ordo pushing their inner limits should be leaving their humanity behind because the Beast's influence isn't the <i>only </i>thing that results in Humanity loss.<br /> <br /> You're saying that the Ordo can't have a Humanity cap because their power doesn't come directly from the Beast, because the cap mechanic comes from the Circle, who <i>do</i> get their power from the Beast, yes? <i>I'm</i> saying that regardless of where their power comes from, the mindset that <i>drives </i>it would be accurately represented by a Humanity cap.<br /> <br /> It's not even so much that the Coils and Scales are corruptive (although those Breaking Points are still there), it's that someone dedicated enough to transcend even mundane undeath is probably going to have a lot of 'em, which is kind of the only metric available for that kind of... uh... personal growth. Their relationship is more correlative than causative, but it's there.<br /> <br /> ...or should be, I guess, is my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words...<br /> <br /> The Circle tries it's best to stress that it's natural and their power comes from the Beast which opposes the Man. Which leads to Cruac drawing it's power from the Beast.<br /> <br /> The Ordo says screw the Beast and kicks the Man to the side to be some ubermensch which leads to problems if you are trying to maintain humanity if you're entire covenant's ethos is basically saying such behavior is for the vermin and sheep.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T04:50:38-07:00","id":528716,"title":"","content":"I just don't see mindset causing a Humanity cap. That's the domain of spiritual corruption.<br /> <br /> For example, in my read of things, and the way I present them in game, Cruac came first, along with its corrupting influence on the Man, and Circle philosophy arose from that. Suffering equals growth and power, so put squeamish concerns aside and embrace suffering. It's not the Acolyte philosophy that caps Humanity. It's Cruac itself. Dark, bloody, hungry Cruac. <br /> <br /> Mindsets can lead to breaking points, sure, but not a guaranteed loss or cap. <br /> <br /> And the Ordo Dracul specifically does not &quot;kick the Man to the side.&quot; At least not as a blanket philosophy. I'm very interested to see their treatment in <i>Secrets of the Covenants.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T04:59:04-07:00","id":528718,"title":"","content":"The Order may kick the Man to the side, but they do it in an entirely mundane, non-mystical way. So the Beast can't dig it's claws in any deeper than it can in any other vamp that falls that low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T07:01:25-07:00","id":528760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528680#post528680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I'm</i> saying that regardless of where their power comes from, the mindset that <i>drives </i>it would be accurately represented by a Humanity cap.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's no way to mechanically represent that for the wide variety of mindsets. What if someone is just following someone else's notes? At the risk of Godwin's Law here, but the whole thing with unethical testing is that it does produce results faster than not. We've pardoned criminals in exchange for notes that save millions of lives in the medical field. That information, once discovered, isn't harming the integrity millions of doctors world wide. Its saving lives.<br /> <br /> The point is - while developing a Scale is likely bad to your Humanity... if you're just <i>taught </i>the Scale? Steal its knowledge via diablarie (which has its own rules), use Dominate or Auspex, something like that? Doesn't make sense. And, even if you go with the evil mad alchemist route, we still have the point that not everyone engages in inhuman acts equally - some acts are more inhuman than others.<br /> <br /> The fact is that, for the most part, there is nothing inhuman about using a Scale. There's not enough of a proximate causation to justify anything related to Humanity here. You want to learn scale, the ST can require you to make inhuman experiments, then hit you with breaking points as you engage in said experiments. Its the actions to justify buying the scale that's the issue, not the scale itself. Because said actions can be so many different things, trying to paint a one-size-fits-all doesn't work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-26-2015, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:25:52-07:00","id":529428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528716#post528716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't see mindset causing a Humanity cap. That's the domain of spiritual corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug*<br /> While it's not perfectly analogous, obviously, I feel that an expectation of Detachment to accompany such a fundamental transformation as rewriting both the Curse and the way you interact with it isn't out of line for the Ordo the way they're written. You describe Cruac as making more room for the Beast at the Man's expense- what I'm imagining doesn't give the Beast any more leeway so much as adapt the Man into something less soft and disingenuous and more durable... at the expense of its relatability to actual humans. Again, obviously, that's a big mechanical change, but it's one I feel completes the implications created by the source material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528718#post528718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Order may kick the Man to the side, but they do it in an entirely mundane, non-mystical way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heheh. Considering their attitude of &quot;evolve or die&quot; and their practice of alchemical do-it-your-self-improvement, would your really call this kind of hypothetical deep-psyche auto-trepanning from Man into Man Plus either mundane <i>or</i> non-mystical? :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=528760#post528760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's no way to mechanically represent that for the wide variety of mindsets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it's pretty inelegant, but everything being equal I don't think it's <i>that </i>poor a way to reflect the default Dragon's changes. About the only other thing I could think of would be to re-introduce Paths, but talk about the cure being worse than the disease &gt;:C","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T04:49:13-07:00","id":529773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=529428#post529428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree it's pretty inelegant, but everything being equal I don't think it's <i>that </i>poor a way to reflect the default Dragon's changes. About the only other thing I could think of would be to re-introduce Paths, but talk about the cure being worse than the disease &gt;:C</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree, I think it is a poor way. First, I know you said this offhandedly, but everything is NOT being equal. Coils and Scales aren't Cruac. Cruac is innately tied to the demonic strix, to communion with the Beast and a primal mind set; I see Coils and Scales as controlling the Beast through academic knowledge and higher brain functions, not primal instinct. Its implied that low Humanity = beastial, not inhuman, and I don't think equating the Ordo to beastial is appropriate, while it is appropriate for the Circle.<br /> <br /> Two, scales have no reason to restrict Humanity once they're known. Learning one from a book or a teacher doesn't require torture to learn (only discover the first time). Hells, even if you wanted to assume using a Scale is detrimental to Humanity by making each use of a scale a breaking point, lets say, not all scales are equal - one that removes blood bonds can sit unused for large swaths of play-time, while one that is used to go out in the sunlight finds constant use. Two people with two different Coils acting in vastly different ways being capped in the same manner? Makes no sense.<br /> <br /> Three, appropriate Banes are more fun and thematic, I think, than a cap, which would discourage players from taking Banes (which happens in my experience). And taking a bane is often far more inhuman in practice, even though it ironically preserves Humanity.<br /> <br /> Instituting a cap has a lot of effects that go just beyond forcing Scale users to degrade in Humanity that I think is clumsy and could hurt the way the covenant is seen and played.<br /> <br /> Let me ask a question. Why do you need to reflect a Dragon's shift in mindset in such a different manner than any of the other covenants? The Invictus change, the Carthians change, the Lance change. If VII includes Kindred and not something stranger, they change too. They don't need a humanity cap, even if they commit as many inhuman acts as the Ordo in their own ways? I mean, really, the Movement is the only covenant that isn't associated with a couple different VtM Paths. All the covenants lead to inhumanity one way or another. Why does the Ordo specifically need one and the others do not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T05:02:16-07:00","id":529802,"title":"","content":"Also if the coils <i>did </i>cap humanity it would just spur them to create more coils that allow one to ignore the effects of lowered humanity.<br /> <br /> So the chief reason for not applying a cap is that it <i>wouldn't work.</i><br /> <br /> In fact, considering that the coils are things the Dragons designed it may well be that any such coil that capped the humanity dots (there are ways of telling in a vague sense) would be rejected as a failure and redesigned until it didn't have that drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 05-27-2015, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:09:39-07:00","id":529911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=529428#post529428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree it's pretty inelegant, but everything being equal I don't think it's <i>that </i>poor a way to reflect the default Dragon's changes. About the only other thing I could think of would be to re-introduce Paths, but talk about the cure being worse than the disease &gt;:C</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think you've hit the crux of my dislike of the cap idea here. What you're talking about isn't erosion of Humanity, because that, in Dragon terms, is called Unreason. One of the three main things they're trying to combat with the Mysteries and Coils. I know that's a 1e concept, and it doesn't fit perfectly with some of the re-imaginings of Frenzy and such in 2e, but the basic concept still holds as a cornerstone for the Coils.<br /> <br /> As Elfive was driving at, creating a direct consequence of the Coils that is one of the very things the Coils are supposed to eliminate is no good.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T07:11:40-07:00","id":529921,"title":"","content":"They DID create effects to expressly boost their effective Humanity or obviate the need for Detachment checks in certain circumstances for practitioners. So that kind of invalidates the theory that the Ordo Dracul gets to nonchalantly ride around on their dragon coils, butchering human and kindred alike in the name of their crusade to overthrow God, immune the spiritual/psychological repercussions reflected by the Humanity and Banes mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T19:12:01-07:00","id":530492,"title":"","content":"I think there is confusion between morality and humanity. Torture is a buzz word. However, torture is not universally bad. Solitary confinement is an example of torture, but it is used to segregate people that are dangerous to others routinely. Ever heard of a bikini wax? That is essentially torture (gets off on a technicality) that women pay to have done. Dragons inflict pain to change themselves or to learn how to change themselves. This concept that pain is an unacceptable aspect to research or treatment is only a few decades old. Despite this, torture is still used in any instance where nothing else works. The difference between water-boarding and nasal irrigation is the purpose for which it is done. A blood bond is in effect equivalent to brain washing so the scale to remove it is a medical treatment, like nasal irrigation. I believe the word was used only to emphasize that it was an unpleasant procedure. It is better characterized as treatment than torture. I don't think any Scale created has to be used as an evil act or an act of torture. Researching Coils and Scales are breaking points, right? Using them is not. Coils and Scales are amoral. They are tools to be used for good or ill. That mass embrace scale being an exception. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T19:30:59-07:00","id":530522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=530492#post530492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is confusion between morality and humanity. Torture is a buzz word. However, torture is not universally bad. Solitary confinement is an example of torture, but it is used to segregate people that are dangerous to others routinely. Ever heard of a bikini wax? That is essentially torture (gets off on a technicality) that women pay to have done. Dragons inflict pain to change themselves or to learn how to change themselves. This concept that pain is an unacceptable aspect to research or treatment is only a few decades old. Despite this, torture is still used in any instance where nothing else works. The difference between water-boarding and nasal irrigation is the purpose for which it is done. A blood bond is in effect equivalent to brain washing so the scale to remove it is a medical treatment, like nasal irrigation. I believe the word was used only to emphasize that it was an unpleasant procedure. It is better characterized as treatment than torture. I don't think any Scale created has to be used as an evil act or an act of torture. Researching Coils and Scales are breaking points, right? Using them is not. Coils and Scales are amoral. They are tools to be used for good or ill. That mass embrace scale being an exception. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your raise some good points, and highlight the important difference between humanity and morality.<br /> <br /> More importantly, you discussed Coils and Scales, bikini waxing, blood bonds, and nasal irrigation all in the same paragraph and still managed to make sense!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T01:40:27-07:00","id":530768,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Making sense is generally a good thing.<br /> <br /> I don't think any of the covenants are very good, hence joining one is a breaking point. All covenants allow really sick bastards to thrive in their ranks. The Ordo Dracul has its share of evil bastards just like the rest. Furthermore, it has plenty more willing to turn a blind eye to the evil of others. However, they do not require a member to be evil. Although there is that whole kill a person and watch what happens exercise. Chasing the Dragon's Tail? The Carthians don't care what you do as long as you pay your dues. The Invictus feel the same way but regarding the Masquerade. The Lancea Sanctum torture people because they think God wills it. All covenants should allow evil to flourish while allowing an individual to retain their humanity as much as they wish. Maybe if that is not clear, the Secrets of the Covenants will provide clarity. Exception being the Circle of the Crone because they aren't real big on humanity, but they still don't require a member to be a sick bastard. You just get perks for being one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T03:01:11-07:00","id":530818,"title":"","content":"That's not why joining a covenant is a breaking point. Breaking points are anything that distances you from your human roots. Living for a long time and surviving something because of your undead constitution are both up there too. Joining a covenant is a breaking point because it means you are voluntarily joining the vampire club for not-humans. You're like, &quot;yep, I am totally a vampire now.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T08:01:04-07:00","id":531015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=530492#post530492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is confusion between morality and humanity. Torture is a buzz word. However, torture is not universally bad. Solitary confinement is an example of torture, but it is used to segregate people that are dangerous to others routinely. Ever heard of a bikini wax? That is essentially torture (gets off on a technicality) that women pay to have done. Dragons inflict pain to change themselves or to learn how to change themselves. This concept that pain is an unacceptable aspect to research or treatment is only a few decades old. Despite this, torture is still used in any instance where nothing else works. The difference between water-boarding and nasal irrigation is the purpose for which it is done. A blood bond is in effect equivalent to brain washing so the scale to remove it is a medical treatment, like nasal irrigation. I believe the word was used only to emphasize that it was an unpleasant procedure. It is better characterized as treatment than torture. I don't think any Scale created has to be used as an evil act or an act of torture. Researching Coils and Scales are breaking points, right? Using them is not. Coils and Scales are amoral. They are tools to be used for good or ill. That mass embrace scale being an exception. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in my initial post, I did call out the Scale for breaking blood bonds as been &quot;acceptable torture.&quot; Because, in theory, you're doing it to free someone from a Blood Bond they don't want. You certainly could use it on someone who's quite happy being bound, break them free so you can take them for yourself, but that would be a whole separate issue.<br /> <br /> You do, indeed, raise a good point that none of the Scales need to be used to do evil. However, using them almost requires you to do evil. Several of them, specifically the ones I called out in my original post, require (often large) amounts of tissue from humans. While it has been rightly pointed out that there are means to acquire those materials that don't rely on killing people for their body parts, it would still generally be a lot easier to kill one person and get all the stuff you need, instead of haunting the local liposuction clinic for a week. One of them specifically requires a large quantity of <i>fresh</i> blood, no more than one minute old, meaning you have to have a &quot;donor&quot; on hand, likely more than one if you don't want to leave dead bodies around. And, of course, few people are willing to part with large quantities of whole blood, so you need to do something to enforce their co-operation.<br /> <br /> Now, I get that this could easily be called &quot;feature&quot; instead of &quot;bug,&quot; but it just rubs me the wrong way. I get that there should be temptation to do &quot;evil&quot; for vampires, but, as I've tried to explain, the presentation leaves me with the impression that the Ordo are less tempted to do evil then they are evil by default. I agree that none of the Covenants are particularly &quot;good,&quot; but I don't like playing them as particularly evil, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T08:16:48-07:00","id":531027,"title":"","content":"I mean, at the end of the day, it's a game about humans who are slowly turning into monsters. The Covenants are formed by characters who have probably been around longer that you and are probably further along their path to monster hood, so it's only appropriate that they would seem evil by human standards, because the people running the show don't have a whole lot of human left in them. As a player, your character doesn't have to become a monster, but the covenants themselves pretty much are all &quot;evil&quot; by default, assuming by &quot;evil&quot; you mean devoid of human moral standards. Individuals are, well, individual, but the organizations are all founded on inherently inhuman ideals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-28-2015, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T08:39:57-07:00","id":531044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=531015#post531015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I get that this could easily be called &quot;feature&quot; instead of &quot;bug,&quot; but it just rubs me the wrong way. I get that there should be temptation to do &quot;evil&quot; for vampires, but, as I've tried to explain, the presentation leaves me with the impression that the Ordo are less tempted to do evil then they are evil by default. I agree that none of the Covenants are particularly &quot;good,&quot; but I don't like playing them as particularly evil, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely call it a feature. One of the quintessential traits of evil is that it's easier than good. It's easier to pick up a vagrant, kill him, exsanguinate him, and skin him for your Scale fixin's. I like that incentive to take the easy, darker path. I like that the door is open for a player whose character is trying to be good to go the extra mile. <br /> <br /> There's a lot of inherent immorality in the Covenants, and I understand that might not be everyone's (your) cup of tea. I suppose I hit the jackpot being among those who are the target audience of the tonal shift/re-imagining in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T15:16:16-07:00","id":531279,"title":"","content":"I don't disagree as a whole you could characterize the Ordo Dracul as more evil than most of the rest, but two points are missed. The first is the Ordo Dracul is composed of three factions; warriors, researchers, judges. Only the research branch needs to be evil. The warriors could be down right heroic. This leaves you with a group that accepts some evil members and supports them.<br /> <br /> This is true of all covenants though. Guess who is a part of the Carthians? Nazi vampires. That means all Carthians support Nazis. Does that make them all evil? It would be like saying ISIS and Muslims are all the same. Just because you let someone else do evil doesn't make you evil. People turn a blind eye all the time. The good members of the Ordo Dracul exist and pretend not to notice what their darker brethren do with their nights.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt was the same with Germans around 1940. If you see trains and trucks full of Jews going to a camp and they are always empty when they leave. You don't see building supplies to expand the camp. What do you think is happening to the Jews? The German people were largely ignorant of the Holocaust because they chose to be. So was the rest of the world. Do we condemn all Germans? All the people of the world at the time? They allowed the Holocaust. They must be evil. They are not evil. They were ignorant. Ignorance is bliss.<br /> <br /> If you play the game out of the box, players will be interacting with sickos. They will work alongside them and defend them at times. They will have to struggle to keep from becoming like them. If you want to move away from that then you need to lighten up all the covenants. Just like most people conveniently leave out the Nazi Carthians. You can lighten up the Ordo Dracul by bringing them out of the shadows. If they are a pretty open group then they will tone down all their evil shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T15:20:20-07:00","id":531280,"title":"","content":"I don't really see why people are saying the Ordo Dracul are more &quot;evil&quot; than everyone else. The value of that statement is debatable in and of itself, but really, look at the company they keep. The other major covenants. Are they REALLY somehow demonstrably MORE 'evil' than the others?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T18:13:36-07:00","id":531468,"title":"","content":"Carthian Law doesn't require &quot;human resources.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T18:21:48-07:00","id":531476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=531468#post531468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carthian Law doesn't require &quot;human resources.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but they use it to enforce their experiments with different Kindred government systems, many of which are just as amoral as anything the Ordo does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T18:27:55-07:00","id":531479,"title":"","content":"In order from &quot;most good&quot; to &quot;most evil&quot; I would put them<br /> <br /> Carthians &gt; Invictus &gt; Lancea Sanctum &gt; Ordo Dracul &gt; Circle of the Crone<br /> <br /> Carthians are on the left because because they don't have any evil practices and unlike the Invictus are not obsessed with their own personal power. Lancea Sanctum are in the middle because they can do good things, but also have some wicked ways. Circle of the Crone are on the right because their practices actually require a stripping away of humanity, and they embrace being monsters. The Ordo Dracul falls where it is due to evil rites without any redeeming ones.<br /> <br /> On a numerical scale the differences would be minute. They are all in the same magnitude of evilness. They also all allow very human, and possibly good and noble, members within their ranks. As a group they are more evil than most, but individually they fall within the norm. They have nothing special to drive them to do ill.<br /> <br /> Demonstrably? Nope. The difference is a shade less than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 05-28-2015, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T18:44:02-07:00","id":531494,"title":"","content":"is &quot;covenant advantage may or may not require things from human beings&quot; really the metric? Last I checked, <i>all </i>vampires require blood to survive, and these are certainly not organizations which promote an &quot;animal exsanguination only&quot; policy by default. Nevermind all the other stuff they do in pursuit of their goals.<br /> <br /> Like really, if unethical science is what it takes to be evil, then the Circle of the Crone has angel wings, the Invictus is just looking out for the little guy, the Carthians are just borrowing some ideas and the Sanctified just want you to say your evening prayers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-28-2015, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:01:05-07:00","id":531523,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think the Lancea et Sanctum is 'more evil' than the Circle. Acolytes, by accepting and even relying on the Beast, often at least have some genuine perspective on what their actions are in relation to who they are, and as such they actually do have boundaries. Add on top of that that through a certain Zen embrace of the Beast, by embracing their Beast, they also sort of actively find a certain amount of their humanity in that. I mean, as a minor note, their <i>wedding</i> ceremony is absolutely touching.<br /> <br /> Lancea et Sanctum has their shepherding of humanity and acceptance of the beast, but then you have their self-righteous justification of everything they do. For all their talk of damnation, they don't really own their actions the way they do in the Circle.<br /> <br /> It's been too long since I've read the Lancea book, where as I keep going back to the Circle, so I know them fairly well, and I also freely admit I have a personal peeve with religious structures justifying shit, but yeah, no, I don't think the Circle is any worse than the Sanctified.<br /> <br /> As for the Ordo, transmonsterism. Yeah, I love these guys, but they're pretty low on the scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:08:08-07:00","id":531528,"title":"","content":"I think comparative morality is a little misdirected when applied to monsters who drink human blood for sustenance and occasionally freak out to the extent they murder everyone in the general vicinity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That aside, I wouldn't say the Carthians are the &quot;good guys&quot;, trying multiple different political systems means that occasionally a model based on fascist tyranny would be applied to test it out. Also, personally, as they're presented, I feel the Circle are as close to a pure antagonist covenant, their embracing of their bestial nature and seeming inhumanity make them hard for me to see in a positive light (as an outside observer of the setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:12:07-07:00","id":531534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=531528#post531528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think comparative morality is a little misdirected when applied to monsters who drink human blood for sustenance and occasionally freak out to the extent they murder everyone in the general vicinity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That aside, I wouldn't say the Carthians are the &quot;good guys&quot;, trying multiple different political systems means that occasionally a model based on fascist tyranny would be applied to test it out. Also, personally, as they're presented, I feel the Circle are as close to a pure antagonist covenant, their embracing of their bestial nature and seeming inhumanity make them hard for me to see in a positive light (as an outside observer of the setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, seriously. THe Carthians might be the most human with their evil side? But they are still really indulging in some serious shitkicking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:12:52-07:00","id":531535,"title":"","content":"But the Beast isn't just a monstrous killer, it can also be competitive or seductive. Plus, they promote freedom of thought and belief, tenets of good guys everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:21:18-07:00","id":531538,"title":"","content":"I still think evil is the absolute silliest metric to judge the Covenants by, but I'm a little but surprised by that. Is this really just a reaction to the perceived self-righteousness of Judeo-Christian vampires? Because they know they're bad, and their church is as much about ordering the Kindred existence as it is proselytizing to heathen vampires.<br /> <br /> I mean sure, the Circle counsels acceptance of the Beast, and that's very good and all for not hating yourself for being Kindred, but I've yet to see anything to indicate the Circle is interested in curbing the, ah, 'ethical excesses' of its membership, whereas Longinian doctrine has some strong words to say on treating the kine like playthings and stuff.<br /> <br /> Insofar as which group is a better bulwark for your humanity, it's probably the Sanctified. That said, neither of them are gonna do a terribly good job keeping your humanity very high, though the Sanctified do seem less likely to destabilize it through regular existence.<br /> <br /> While I don't know how useful the 1st edition covenant books are in discussing their 2nd edition behavior, the Sanctified MO seems to still fit somewhat with these basic ideas of what the Testament provides for.<br /> <br /> I'll also admit that I've got a personal bugbear when it comes to them because I've seen a lot of people assume that the Circle are better people because they're not Vampire Christians. I'm definitely not saying the Sanctified <i>aren't </i>judgmental assholes, they just seem to be more <i>humane </i>judgmental assholes compared with their pagan<i>ish</i> counterparts in the Circle. You and I might have a decidedly negative view of religious power structures, but that on its own doesn't actually make the Sanctified worse than the others.<br /> <br /> I think they're both really cool groups, but I often feel that the Sanctified get sold short with people because of a negative view of Christianity and its derivatives.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Thinking about it, I realize it's sort of two different issues. The Crones might help you accept your Kindred nature more easily (though evidently the Sanctified doctrine can do similar) but the Circle just doesn't really have any provisions for humanity or restrictions on behaviors that are suggestive of any kind of order. They buck that trend, and that's gonna look a lot like conventional evil/selfishness because it facilitates those things. That's really my argument against considering them more moral or less evil than the Sanctified, because part of their <i>thing </i>seems to be a reaction against the doctrine of groups like the Sanctified, which enforce an order and restriction on Kindred behavior. That doctrine happens to include things like protecting the flock and not being excessively abusive towards humans, and the Crones do no such thing. Their cruelty is unfettered, and that seems to be in part because their beliefs about themselves and the Beast justify it.<br /> <br /> One way or another, you're justifying bad behavior. There's just examples of what you <i>shouldn't </i>do in Sanctified doctrine, while the Circle doesn't seem to care about that sort of thing. If we have to put conventional morality on organizations made for, and by, and for the benefit of vampires, (I don't wanna!) the Sanctified at least have some kind of provisions about abusing people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-28-2015, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:28:35-07:00","id":531547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=531538#post531538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I've yet to see anything to indicate the Circle is interested in curbing the, ah, 'ethical excesses' of its membership</div> </div> </div> </div>They believe the descent is important, as 'the natural progress of a healthy vampire,' but it's also important to appreciate what one has lost, and not abandon oneself to the Beast. True appreciation of the vampire condition, to them, is only possible when one has very little humanity to cling to left.<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood comments upon this, as they believe the Circle are essentially cowards, those who look upon the precipice of losing their humanity and balk. They're degenerates, who take the gifts granted by their abandoning of humanity, then loaf around and preen while using them and not appreciating the lessons and advancement.<br /> <br /> There's also the comparisons to natural phenomena. Parasite to host. Predator to prey. As they are part of a natural cycle, upending the natural balance of things is frowned upon. Parasites cannot exist without their host, and if a host notices its parasite, it may dig it out. Predators have nothing to predate without their prey, and if the prey are cornered, they may retaliate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One way or another, you're justifying bad behavior. </div> </div> </div>Whether it causes humanity loss is not the the sole factor in whether something is bad or not. In many cases, it's not a factor at all. A vampire can re-enact the Jonestown massacre without dropping below 6. Alternatively, a vampire can drop to 1 solely by 'living' a long time, harming no one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-28-2015, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T19:44:27-07:00","id":531571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=531547#post531547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They believe the descent is important, as 'the natural progress of a healthy vampire,' but it's also important to appreciate what one has lost, and not abandon oneself to the Beast. True appreciation of the vampire condition, to them, is only possible when one has very little humanity to cling to left.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have deathday parties for this reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T20:15:39-07:00","id":531621,"title":"","content":"If we're derailing into a discussion on the Circle versus the Sanctum, I'd like to examine this idea that &quot;one way or another, you're justifying bad behavior.&quot; I think that's exactly what it is, and why I'm not inclined to put Sanctum above (maybe not below, either) the Circle morally.<br /> <br /> Namely: don't the Sanctum and Circle both believe and act on the idea that they are, at the core of their nature, both monsters?<br /> <br /> The only real difference here (from my knowledge of 2e only) seems to me whether they think they are blessed by the Old Gods or cursed by the New. They both see themselves as monsters. They both see it their role in unlife to act on that monstrous nature. Maybe the Sanctum directs that monstrosity towards a higher purpose (this is where it becomes iffy whether they'd rank 'below' the Crone; I'm inclined to think so), but it's still the same core worldview as the Circle with different decorations and litanies.<br /> <br /> The goal for the Sanctum is to tempt humanity and be a thorn in its side. The goal for the Circle is to accept and be in-tune with their inner monster. The reasons behind these goals are the same for both; they were made monsters by something of religious nature and have an obligation to their divine to act as they do. The end results of both are probably some mortals caught in the crossfire.<br /> <br /> Indeed, back to the topic of this thread, membership in the Sanctum at least necessitates the suffering of mortals, whereas the Ordo can do everything their Covenant requires of them without ever seeing living kine at all. The 2e books thus far are vague, but it seems like the Circle doesn't necessitate interaction with mortals at all. Invictus certainly doesn't. Carthians probably don't have to, but their fluff and in-book fiction indicate they are usually involved heavily with mortals on a social level. This interaction often ends in a feeding/siring frenzy if the text is to be taken as representative. I also don't buy the idea that they aren't interested in personal power; they're vampires, of course they are. But that's neither here nor there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T01:00:03-07:00","id":531787,"title":"","content":"I really really dislike the idea of ranking the covenants from &quot;most evil&quot; to &quot;least evil&quot;. All of them are fucked up in their own ways. All of them are evil. Especially the Carthians. And the Lance. And the Invictus. And the Circle. And the Ordo.<br /> <br /> I am not even talking about how much such a ranking takes away from the game, when one group becomes demonstrably better than another. <br /> <br /> I","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T02:24:31-07:00","id":531808,"title":"","content":"You might want to continue reading after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T03:01:47-07:00","id":531819,"title":"","content":"I did. Providing arguments why one is better than the other ignores a lot of the points of why the argument is wrong. You provided your comparison, saying that Carthians are best, Circle is the worst, but you also amended that with saying that &quot;the difference is small.&quot;<br /> I say that's completely subjective and has little basis in what covenants really are. I could write up the exact opposite chart (where Circle is the best and Carthians are the worst), provide the arguments which would defend the opinion and then say &quot;but the difference is small.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T05:09:36-07:00","id":531851,"title":"","content":"I have to agree. Especially since it's been clear since the start that representations of the covenants vary from city to city, as do members, and a covenant is just an organization and has no moral alignment.<br /> <br /> Everyone's entitled to their views, but just deciding who's evil and who's not or who's more evil and who's more good ignores a lot about the game. That's not even taking into account the fact that it doesn't matter. Each covenant is demonstrably playable. Each covenant has their good side and bad side. The choice of covenant for their character has no reflection on the moral qualities of the player, and a player character is equally capable of being an absolute monster or an absolute saint in any of the five primary covenants, and you don't need the powers a covenant bestows to murder, rape, lie, cheat, steal, or start a human trafficking ring, these are all things people are capable of doing without a vampire social club. We've discussed how the Ordo Dracul actually works. One scale is tantamount to torture? If your player or character finds this so objectionable, they are free not to learn it. If they find it so objectionable that they refuse to join the covenant? That's fine for them.<br /> <br /> But one's own moral beliefs should not be forced on others, especially in and about a game. It has no bearing beyond your table, unless you wanted to just get people's opinions on what they think, which this thread is clearly not doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-29-2015, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T06:46:35-07:00","id":531927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=531494#post531494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is &quot;covenant advantage may or may not require things from human beings&quot; really the metric? Last I checked, <i>all </i>vampires require blood to survive, and these are certainly not organizations which promote an &quot;animal exsanguination only&quot; policy by default. Nevermind all the other stuff they do in pursuit of their goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather different kettle of fish. Vampires are supposed to feed carefully and discreetly, and done properly, the victim will never realize exactly what happened. Now, sure, vampires can go out and drain the first random person they meet every night, but that's not exactly the brightest thing to do.<br /> <br /> Scales require large amounts of human tissue, most of which has to be extract surgically. So if you're not getting medical biohazard refuse, at best you're killing someone and literally butchering them like an animal to get skin, fat, etc. Worst-case, you've got a bunch of humans bound in your basement, and carve chunks out of their still-living bodies whenever you need materials for a new experiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T09:35:36-07:00","id":532011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=531927#post531927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scales require large amounts of human tissue, most of which has to be extract surgically. So if you're not getting medical biohazard refuse, at best you're killing someone and literally butchering them like an animal to get skin, fat, etc. Worst-case, you've got a bunch of humans bound in your basement, and carve chunks out of their still-living bodies whenever you need materials for a new experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>The coil that uses human skin is to heal aggravated damage. Unless a vampire is a masochist, they are not likely to need a constant influx of skin. Though if you did need one, actual doctors do collect skin to be used for skin grafts, and nothing keeps a vampire from using the same method, that of removing the skin off corpses. The coil can also be used on humans to allow them to heal lethal damage faster.<br /> <br /> As we've established, <a href=\"http://blogs.discovermagazine.com/80beats/2012/04/06/how-do-scientists-get-ahold-of-human-fat-tummy-tucks/\" target=\"_blank\">human fat can be obtained without harm to anyone</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-29-2015, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T15:01:27-07:00","id":532371,"title":"","content":"I personally think of covenants as &quot;clan mentalities.&quot; The Ordo Dracul has a lot in common with the way Mehket think and act - gathering information, mystery cults, etc. The CotC almost panders to how the Gangrel think and act. The Lance feels very Nosferatu - we are all monsters - to me. Ventrue Invictrus and Carthian Daeva are cliches for a reason. ((Ghouls and VII? Stix and Brood?))<br /> <br /> So, to me, the question of &quot;which are the most evil covenants&quot; asks &quot;what are the worst vampire clans&quot; as well. Nightmares, brainwashing, thought policing, rule of the strong... Take your pick. What's your worst approach to the Requiem? That's all personal preference. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I want to go back and address the idea that covenants are all &quot;evil.&quot; Now, the presentation is of a bunch of bad people. No arguments. However, I'd like to point over to the Changeling previews we've got going on. Seemings, we're told, are the one part of the game where we CAN'T have it be about abuse. Its where we highlight the success and triumph over adversity. Covenants are like that in Vampire, I think. Its the one area of the game that's really pushing the dark aspects of the game. I'm not getting the same vampire excess from the other parts of the book. So, the Covenants are highlighting the bads, while other parts highlight the good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:55:47-07:00","id":532639,"title":"","content":"I ranked them based on their ideologies which is objective, but only valid in a &quot;white room&quot; which is why I went on to say how small the difference really was because in a practical sense they would only be different based on a subjective basis. The ranking was in response to the query of how the Ordo Dracul could be considered worse than others. I might not have been as clear as I should have been as I get tired of repeating myself. I guess the reasoning just wasn't clear. I was not ranking them in a practical sense which as you suggest. As you said, that would be entirely subjective. I said they were not demonstrably different because there really was no basis to argue with the ranking. It was a piece of the whole. Disregard it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T08:27:25-07:00","id":533230,"title":"","content":"It is worthy of note that no Ordo member needs Scales. Scales provide the uninitiated the benefit of your Coil, and are not needed to advance in your Coil/Mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T21:36:44-07:00","id":534004,"title":"","content":"Just a thought about the Scales of the Ascendant. I just realized after seeing a commercial for cosmetic surgery, how easy it would be for a vampire to get human fat and skin tissue. Liposuction and a tummy tuck anyone? Just dominate or ghoul your local plastic surgeon. No worries about losing humanity, some humans would actually call it improving their lives.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4380-blunt_force_trauma","name":"Blunt_Force_Trauma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T05:50:20-07:00","id":534236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=533230#post533230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is worthy of note that no Ordo member needs Scales. Scales provide the uninitiated the benefit of your Coil, and are not needed to advance in your Coil/Mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div> But you don't need Coils to learn Scales either, nor are Scales or Coils necessary for any of the other things in the Secrets of the Covenant preview. The Ordo, unlike Lance or Circle, isn't all-eggs-in-one-sorcery-basket. They're very much the sum of all their different parts working in synergy. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T08:34:39-07:00","id":534372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=534236#post534236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But you don't need Coils to learn Scales either</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I could have sworn you did, but when you said this I had to double-check, and you totally don't! That's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T18:22:10-07:00","id":534991,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=529773#post529773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I know you said this offhandedly, but everything is NOT being equal. Coils and Scales aren't Cruac. Its implied that low Humanity = beastial, not inhuman, and I don't think equating the Ordo to beastial is appropriate, while it is appropriate for the Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=529773#post529773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"></div> </div> </div> </div>Hence approximation<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, yes. If anyone has a suggestion beyond &quot;swallow a minor to moderate discrepancy because your fix is ugly and implies an identical origin to the Circle's unique mechanic&quot; then I would absolutely welcome it- I hate slogging around in crunchfluff slurry as much as everybody seems to hate me doing it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=529773#post529773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Let me ask a question. Why do you need to reflect a Dragon's shift in mindset in such a different manner than any of the other covenants? The Invictus change, the Carthians change, the Lance change. Why does the Ordo specifically need one </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Covenants aren't just social clubs or a means of mutual protection- they're ways for vampires to deal with their new selves, in one way or another. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Invictus and the Carthians opposites regarding the &quot;what should society be like&quot; axis, so in this regard they're separate from the &quot;personal development&quot; issues discussed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Circle and the LeS are opposites on the &quot;what should </span></span></span><i>we </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">be like&quot; axis. One deals with rising inhumanity by stressing that while the Beast is a necessary evil, one that has a purpose and should be expressed, it's one that needs to be tightly controlled beyond its religious &quot;scourge of god&quot; implications. One deals with rising inhumanity by stressing that the Beast is natural and good and, to a point, should be embraced, because anything else denies your true nature. Both provide reassurance that being monstrous is okay, both have implications on the Man vs. Beast identity issue, and both have magic that provides a tangible example of their philosophy.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Here's where I feel the problem comes from. Dragons have the same &quot;what should we be&quot; concern and the same &quot;philosophy turned outwards(-ish)&quot; magic- but the Man-Beast axis only has two points. They've already been filled by the Manly covenant, which <i>requires </i>high(er) Humanity, and the Beastly covenant, which <i>enforces </i>low(er) Humanity. They're even mirrored on the 0-10 Humanity scale, a floor of 1-5 vs. a ceiling of 9-5. Despite their emphasis on transhumanism, hubris, embrace of change over stasis, and implications of casual cruelty, Dragons became the odd man out Humanity-wise... not because their mentality wouldn't ping Detachment, but because it 1) didn't do so in a manner consistent with the Man vs. Beast philosophy that underlies the both Man-Beast axis and the Humanity system itself, and 2) the Circle <i>did. </i><i>Better</i>. By design, no less.<br /> <br /> Given a bunch of rather amoral, extremely ambitious experimentalists faced with the undignified complication of being saddled with a foaming monster in their head for eternity, yes, I feel their relationship with Humanity should be impacted, somehow, <i>anyhow</i>, beyond &quot;You've successfully kept a human brain alive in a jar using a Vitae-modified nutrient fluid. Gross. Roll for Detachment&quot;. Reading the Dragons' fluff and ignoring absolutely everything Humanity-related except specific instances of Detachment just sits wrong, with me. Frankly, so does a Humanity cap, because, yes, messing with that clean Circle-LeS Beast-Man symmetry for the sake of shoehorning in a much more complex identity-morality issue irritates the everloving <i>shit </i>out of me, but at least it acknowledges that there's a change to be made. One that I keep hoping somebody else will make, only better, because <i>clearly </i>I don't patch very well.<br /> <br /> So. When I talk about a Humanity cap, it's not because I feel the Ordo has the same issues as the Circle, in scale or quality- it's because the idea of trying to turn an axis into a triangle makes me want to gnash my teeth until my jaw falls out.<br /> <br /> <br /> *sigh*<br /> <br /> ...or maybe I just miss the Tzimisce and I never realized it until now.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 05-31-2015, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T19:10:33-07:00","id":535007,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=529802#post529802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if the coils <i>did </i>cap humanity it would just spur them to create more coils that allow one to ignore the effects of lowered humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=529802#post529802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So the chief reason for not applying a cap is that it <i>wouldn't work.</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In fact, considering that the coils are things the Dragons designed it may well be that any such coil that capped the humanity dots (there are ways of telling in a vague sense) would be rejected as a failure and redesigned until it didn't have that drawback. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\\:-| ...your argument is that altering the Dragons' overall approach to Humanity is pointless because they can't not succeed in surmounting <i>any </i>negative effects? The Coils <i>don't</i> offset Humanity limitations any more. Nobody ever said the Coils had perfect, infinite utility, especially given B&amp;S's focus on weaponizing their own drawbacks.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=529911#post529911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Elfive was driving at, creating a direct consequence of the Coils that is one of the very things the Coils are supposed to eliminate is no good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn it. <i>So </i>close. Re-introducing a Humanity coil to reflect a purposefully re-structured consciousness would be elegant, but it just becomes an xp tax if it was the Coils that drew you away in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...I don't know, maybe just re-introduce a Humanity Coil fluffed &quot;beyond morality&quot; and screw messing with their specific approach to Humanity or the cap or whatever. That just goes back to ignoring their ability to cheerfully hacksaw their way through their Requiem as long as you don't draw too much meta-attention to it, of course, but I'm getting sick of round pegs and square holes. Maybe let them trade off their any Humanity lost via egregious bodily science for xp and file the loss under &quot;research, comma, inhumane&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hm. Given 2.0's preference for taking lemons and making combustible lemons, what would a Coil for transhuman mentality look like, do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T19:13:45-07:00","id":535008,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Coil of Ziva has been designed already for exactly this, though we haven't seen a second draft of it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T19:18:25-07:00","id":535037,"title":"","content":"Since vampires already have a way to alter their humanity breaking points, via taking of banes, perhaps said coil would do something with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T19:19:22-07:00","id":535051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=535007#post535007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn it. <i>So </i>close. Re-introducing a Humanity coil to reflect a purposefully re-structured consciousness would be elegant, but it just becomes an xp tax if it was the Coils that drew you away in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;so close.&quot; I wasn't talking about a Coil to deal with Humanity loss. <br /> <br /> I was arguing against a Humanity cap as consequence for the Coils, since one of the things the Coils are supposed to mitigate is the effect of the Beast taking over. Not trying to bring it up again, just clarifying the point.<br /> <br /> Though as Leetsepeak says, Coil of Ziva. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:01:48-07:00","id":535130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=535051#post535051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;so close.&quot; I wasn't talking about a Coil to deal with Humanity loss.<br /> I was arguing against a Humanity cap as consequence for the Coils, since one of the things the Coils are supposed to mitigate is the effect of the Beast taking over. Not trying to bring it up again, just clarifying the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I meant taking what I would have preferred to be a fundamentally different approach to how the other Covenants approach Humanity and instead handwaving it as a Coil because I couldn't figure out any other goddamn way for it to work smoothly would have been much more acceptable... except that you end up double-dipping the Ordo's ice cream in failsauce without providing any commensurate improvement. One of the reasons I wasn't super happy porting the cap/breaking point for Cruac was because the power and versatility of Cruac make a much better carrot to Humanity's stick than the Coils would have. I didn't bring it up because I didn't want to get accused of pushing to beef up the Coils compared to Cruac :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=535051#post535051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though as Leetsepeak says, Coil of Ziva.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I haven't read up on it because I assumed it was homebrew, for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:03:41-07:00","id":535132,"title":"","content":"Ah, it's from <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i>. The first draft at least is in the playtest doc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T09:41:14-07:00","id":535681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=534991#post534991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given a bunch of rather amoral, extremely ambitious experimentalists faced with the undignified complication of being saddled with a foaming monster in their head for eternity, yes, I feel their relationship with Humanity should be impacted, somehow, <i>anyhow</i>, beyond &quot;You've successfully kept a human brain alive in a jar using a Vitae-modified nutrient fluid. Gross. Roll for Detachment&quot;. Reading the Dragons' fluff and ignoring absolutely everything Humanity-related except specific instances of Detachment just sits wrong, with me. Frankly, so does a Humanity cap, because, yes, messing with that clean Circle-LeS Beast-Man symmetry for the sake of shoehorning in a much more complex identity-morality issue irritates the everloving <i>shit </i>out of me, but at least it acknowledges that there's a change to be made. One that I keep hoping somebody else will make, only better, because <i>clearly </i>I don't patch very well.<br /> <br /> So. When I talk about a Humanity cap, it's not because I feel the Ordo has the same issues as the Circle, in scale or quality- it's because the idea of trying to turn an axis into a triangle makes me want to gnash my teeth until my jaw falls out.<br /> <br /> <br /> *sigh*<br /> <br /> ...or maybe I just miss the Tzimisce and I never realized it until now.</div> </div> </div> </div> A few thoughts. First, I'd like to point out that while the Tzim are very much part of the Ordo Dracul's as their spiritual predecessors, so are the Tremere and the Inconnu/Salubri (specifically as Annoshka's Sworn of the Ladder faction in 1e). The Ordo needs to resonate along all three lines without excluding any of them. In 1e, those alien mind sets were made possible through various coils indirectly messing with Humanity. Not its score, but what each level means. In 2e, I would suggest associating the different mind sets based on what Coil you favor - the Tremere favor Voivoid, the Tzimisce the Beast, and the Inconnu the Ascendant. Use affinity powers and scales to encourage the appropriate mindset. <br /> <br /> Secondly, I think you underestimate the effect of Invictus and Carthians, dismissing them out of hand too easily. Both favor large scale mind control and psychological abuse - how is hollowing out someone's mind like the opening in the Estate's fiction less horrific than the body experiments of the Ordo? If we want to do VtM comparisons, the Invictus would be following the Road of the King, for instance. Carthians are the only ones who really stick with the VtM equivalent of Humanity in mindset. <br /> <br /> Third, I really think you need to stop trying to turn the Ordo into the third angle of the sorcery. They just flat out don't fit into the axis - they're too different in not only how they interact with Humanity, but how their powers work, the fact that the Ordo is not a religion, and the nature of Coils is to overcome banes. If the Brood still exist as a covenant, they'd fit nicely as anti-Ordo with how their Investments work, though now they've been swallowed up as a branch of the Lane. Right now, the Ordo are basically a wild card that doesn't favor any one faction on either the political or religion axis. Though, you could rework VII to becoming the anti-Ordo on the evolution-axis, which is actually a pretty interesting discussion we can talk about another time if interested.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=535007#post535007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Coils <i>don't</i> offset Humanity limitations any more.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, the Ascendant Coils and Scales pretty much do just that. There are a few effects of humanity - dealing with fire/sunlight banes, the clan/humanity banes, and a few social penalties. Ascendant takes care of the former fairly effectively. Nothing for the latter two yet, though Ziva has potential, and we can easily make a Scale that does what we need. Voivode already ignores the degenerative aspects of making ghouls, revenants, and childer. <br /> <br /> It should be noted that Ziva is incomplete even on the playtest document (missing a level or two), and will likely change what we do have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hm. Given 2.0's preference for taking lemons and making combustible lemons, what would a Coil for transhuman mentality look like, do you think? </div> </div> </div> Coil of the Wyrm. At high enough levels, you can effectively permanently stay in frenzy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T15:33:07-07:00","id":536018,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=535681#post535681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I'd like to point out that while the Tzim are very much part of the Ordo Dracul's as their spiritual predecessors, so are the Tremere and the Inconnu/Salubri</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah, but IMO the &quot;default&quot; Dragon portrayal tends to come out as the first if they Coil Up, the second if they don't- and since Covenant disciplines are half the fun...</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'll freely admit that it's their </span></span></span><i>general </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">image </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">that comes across as so Tzim, though, rather than specific characters or Clan roles.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN;n535681[/SIZE</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Secondly, I think you underestimate the effect of Invictus and Carthians, dismissing them out of hand too easily. Both favor large scale mind control and psychological abuse - how is hollowing out someone's mind like the opening in the Estate's fiction less horrific than the body experiments of the Ordo? </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bluntly? I feel like the Humanity scale stresses&quot;hard&quot; assaults for Detachment. Don't get me wrong, it's </span></span></span><i>great </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">to finally see mental coercion ping the scale, but they're way up there, compared to physical violence, and even extreme violations of memory and ego that don't directly influence consent require ST fiat to spin into Detachment. I was never sure whether it was to encourage players to do awful things because, hey, look, they're not on the list, right? or whether it was just a word count thing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=535681#post535681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Third, I really think you need to stop trying to turn the Ordo into the third angle of the sorcery.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah, no, that ship has sailed. ]:-( It would be a thing of beauty to make it work, not to mention <i>intensely </i>personally satisfying, but I imagine it would take a heavy redesign, not a fix, to make it work.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=535681#post535681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coil of the Wyrm</div> </div> </div> </div>Guh. &gt;;-P What would a transhuman mentality that <i>doesn't </i>involve turning the Beast into a blunt instrument look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 06-01-2015, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T21:22:27-07:00","id":536469,"title":"","content":"The sample breaking points are not exhaustive nor comprehensive, and they encourage you to move things around as you feel necessary explicitly in the section where it's introduced. Something very important to keep in mind, detachment isn't one of those hardlining things, like Frenzy it's all about what's dramatically appropriate. The sample list is just that, a sample list to help you if you have a hard time parsing that sort of thing out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T08:10:07-07:00","id":537015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=536018#post536018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah, but IMO the &quot;default&quot; Dragon portrayal tends to come out as the first if they Coil Up, the second if they don't- and since Covenant disciplines are half the fun...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'll freely admit that it's their </span></span></span><i>general </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">image </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">that comes across as so Tzim, though, rather than specific characters or Clan roles.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> The stereotypical Dragon portrayal is the student of occult lore. What KIND of student of occult lore depends on what Coils you look after, and your method of developing them - the stereotypical Dragon dabbles in blood alchemy, but also dabbles in wrym nests, geomancy, and ghost-lore. I don't consider that to default to Tzim-like at all for their general image.<br /> <br /> Certainly, I'm looking at the Ordo writeup - I see Frances and Richard exploring the haunted house for occult energies. I do see the occult archaeologist, and the ritualist with his cult of occult dabblers. I see vampires joining because they want to be like human-like again.<br /> <br /> There's a lot going on here, and I don't think that the Tzim is the stereotype - its frankly too restrictive for what the Ordo encompasses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bluntly? I feel like the Humanity scale stresses&quot;hard&quot; assaults for Detachment. Don't get me wrong, it's </span></span></span><i>great </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">to finally see mental coercion ping the scale, but they're way up there, compared to physical violence, and even extreme violations of memory and ego that don't directly influence consent require ST fiat to spin into Detachment. I was never sure whether it was to encourage players to do awful things because, hey, look, they're not on the list, right? or whether it was just a word count thing.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> To an extent, you are right, but in a way that completely misses the point. The vast majority of attacks that serve as breaking points involve killing people, and the one that doesn't? Impassioned violence. Impassioned violence / killing would likely be the result of the Beast being hungry for all that yummy blood, a frenzy situation. Killing, in general, is also inhuman - we are biologically wired to not kill other humans, it requires dehumanizing others to make it really work, and after, it has a lot of psychological trama; and that's for humans. How frenzy situations and murder not strengthen the Beast?<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, there is actually nothing on the Humanity chart for the clinically detached Ordo scientist inflicting pain on a subject. Its very easy to keep them alive - just ghoul them and feed them vitae. Should it be a Humanity hit? Yes. Does it match up to anything on the chart? No. The Humanity chart is not all inclusive - they hit all the ones that are likely to come up - all vampires fall into frenzy and attack people. All vampires eventually kill someone through fenzy at least. All vampires struggle with idea that the expedient way of dealing with problems (rival vamps, human Masq breaches, etc) are to remove them through death. There's nothing specific here that only some vampires will touch, but others won't. Mental damage via disciplines depends on characters - not everyone has the necessary discipline (non-affinity for 40%), making it a more of a niche situation, like clinical torture.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Guh. &gt;;-P What would a transhuman mentality that <i>doesn't </i>involve turning the Beast into a blunt instrument look like? </div> </div> </div> Except its not a blunt instrument. Riding the Wave, at will, is actually a very powerful social tool, especially when Lashing Out comes into play. I've played a Majesty-Nightmare specialist with Coil of the Wyrm as a social character to great effect. It provides a way to ensure that you don't become angry and lose control. The Beast just wants to make the problem go away - ride the wave so you pick how the problem stops, then fall out of frenzy naturally. Plus, the Lashing Out bonus helps keep you from having someone just ignore your disciplines. <br /> <br /> It actively made the character completely and utterly vampire-zen in personality. They didn't get angry or upset, at least on the surface, but they could fix any problem in a seemingly detached manner instead of a RAWR! YOU MADE ME ANGRY! way, creepy little smile and everything. The new Wyrm Coil takes the old Beast Coil outside, and shoots it, then leaves it in the trash for controlling your emotions. Who needs Touchstones to talk you down, when you end frenzy at will? And good luck mentally swaying them. It seems to give you perfect control over your emotions.<br /> <br /> I used to feel the same way you do about the Coils and stuff, until I tried playing an Ordo socialite character. It just clicked really well. And you have no idea how much I'm looking forwards to making an Elysium-style place out of a Wyrms Nest with the new merits. The Invictus may have social connections via Oaths, and the Carthians may have funky Law-enforcement powers, but when it comes down to being a one-vampire charismatic force, the Ordo is the best way to go, imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:00:44-07:00","id":537517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=537015#post537015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It actively made the character completely and utterly vampire-zen in personality. They didn't get angry or upset, at least on the surface, but they could fix any problem in a seemingly detached manner instead of a RAWR! YOU MADE ME ANGRY! way, creepy little smile and everything. The new Wyrm Coil takes the old Beast Coil outside, and shoots it, then leaves it in the trash for controlling your emotions. Who needs Touchstones to talk you down, when you end frenzy at will? And good luck mentally swaying them. It seems to give you perfect control over your emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been rewatching Hemlock Grove recently, and this description actually made me think Dr. Johann Pryce would be a perfect example of an Ordo Dracul, and one who has mastered the Coil of the Wyrm. If, you know, he were a vampire. But his personality and demeanor and 'power' (he has an alleged adrenal gland problem that effectively has him in a controlled Frenzy at all times) is pretty much exactly as you described. I'd hoped to find a good clip to illustrate, but unfortunately could not find one. Hopefully some others know what I'm talking about. The show has a very World of Darkness feel, even if it got a lot of bad reviews. I enjoy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T17:51:55-07:00","id":537541,"title":"","content":"I love that character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T07:18:39-07:00","id":548497,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hopefully this thread is still active so I can get my two cents in. I haven't read through everything yet (only near the end of page 1. Holy poop there's a lot to read but it's fantastic! (Also, I'm hoping that I'm right in the fact that when you say 2E, you mean Blood &amp; Smoke. I'm still fairly scrubbish to these forums)).<br /> <br /> Anyways, I just simply wanted to say that with Science (yes, I consider the Ordo very scientific when it comes to coils/scales), progress demands sacrifice! I'm sure there are a lot out there that are simply inquisitive in nature and explore what possibilities there are. Think Walter/Massive Dynamic from Fringe. They have a theory, they work with it. Occasionally you find something else along the way and roll with it. Science, funnily enough, is not an exact science when inquisitive minds enter the fray!<br /> <br /> \u200bHope that helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T08:42:51-07:00","id":548694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525825-the-ordo-dracul-in-2e?p=548497#post548497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, I'm hoping that I'm right in the fact that when you say 2E, you mean Blood &amp; Smoke. I'm still fairly scrubbish to these forums)).</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. Blood and Smoke (and the God Machine Chronicles book) was originally a trial run to see if a second edition had traction within in the community. It was, so now we're coming out with all new 2nd edition stuff, including a 2nd edition WoD core book. Blood and Smoke was even renamed to Requiem 2nd Edition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}